1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:02:03,570
Visit our website for more: turkision.com

2
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:08,410
No living being was harmed during
the filming of this series.

3
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,799
They beat you.

4
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,919
If you weren't there with the
captive commanders,

5
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:22,919
I wouldn't leave
that place in one piece, Osman Bey.

6
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:26,039
But you came just in time.

7
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:31,319
Didn't you ever think about what
if Nayman hit us both?

8
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:52,599
Martyrdom is the highest position.

9
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,719
May our valiants be in heaven.

10
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:57,949
Amin

11
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,159
We'll destroy you and your family Osman!

12
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:02,479
Stop. Stop.

13
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:06,399
Osman!
Cowards! Untie us!

14
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:12,159
Nayman will be the end of you Osman!

15
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,999
He'll be your end!

16
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:17,199
We'll destroy you and your family!

17
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,479
Is that so?

18
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,959
Come on!

19
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:29,119
Let us how we are going to do it!
We'll drink the blood of your sons!

20
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:31,919
We'll drink their bloods!

21
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:36,639
- Osman!
- I'll bathe in your blood!

22
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:39,799
Will you give
a duty to your children?

23
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,199
- You are all going to die!
- Yes.

24
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:44,239
All of you!

25
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:50,639
My Bey!

26
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:59,429
- I'll show you!
- We'll tear you apart!

27
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:03,879
- Does the traning wait for us, Bey?
- Not training.

28
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:14,519
The working man does not rust, sons.

29
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,839
Since the intelligence is good,

30
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:21,559
then we'll see.
Let's go! Untie their hands!

31
00:04:54,720 --> 00:05:00,169
If I pity, then they become pitiful.

32
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:02,179
I won't pity them.

33
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:04,119
Thanks.

34
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:55,159
- My Bey!
- Wait.

35
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:42,199
Mashallah!

36
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:54,239
Get them and take them away.

37
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:07,359
Sons, this is how you
seem weak...

38
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:12,439
and encourage the enemy. Then,
they will make mistakes.

39
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,879
May you live long.

40
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:18,759
My Bey.

41
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:23,919
You put us in training without hearing
about the news we brought from Bursa.

42
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:28,359
It seems training is
more important than Bursa.

43
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:31,479
My sons are more important than the city.

44
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:34,519
First, get skilled and be strong.

45
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:38,839
Then, many cities and many
castles will be laid before you.

46
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:47,159
Now is not the time, Baysungur.
Not now.

47
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:52,319
Now, let's see how skillful
you are when you are tired.

48
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:58,319
Tell me. Tell me
about Bursa's situation.

49
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:00,319
Come here.

50
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,957
Bursa's Lord, Hadrat Valens.

51
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,879
Dear God.

52
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:29,639
Everyone around me greets you.

53
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:36,879
May your endless grace...

54
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:40,439
always be with us believers.

55
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:42,519
Amen.

56
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:50,399
Our blood sheds for God.

57
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:56,519
We live to kill the enemies of Jesus.

58
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,079
Welcome!

59
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,879
What do we know?

60
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:11,639
Nayman is a descendant of a
warrior Bey of the Belgen tribe.

61
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:16,839
His father is one of the elders of the Beys.
He was always loyal to the Khans.

62
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:23,359
So, what's the difference between
Nayman and his father?

63
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:36,559
Nayman is only loyal to himself.

64
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:41,039
And to his religion.

65
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:44,799
Nayman rebelled against Ghazan Khan...

66
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:49,799
because he led armies in
the East and the West.

67
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:54,239
He grew up but...

68
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:57,679
he always hid his real purpose.

69
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:02,599
Now he wants to destroy Ghazan.

70
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:07,079
If Ghazan Khan is blind to see this,
then he deserves to be destroyed.

71
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:09,959
Let them destroy each other, sir.

72
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:16,639
It is clear from your sentences...

73
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:20,359
that you are the one who
is blind, dear Vasilius.

74
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:26,359
Nayman will come to us.

75
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:30,339
If we don't pick the right side...

76
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,559
we'll be the ones who's
going to be crushed.

77
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:37,039
What about Osman? He's
fighting against Nayman.

78
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,759
That is the reason Nayman will
come here.

79
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:43,159
He'll want to be alliances against Osman.

80
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:48,799
We know everything about Osman's past.

81
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:54,959
What about his future? Do we
know what is he going to do?

82
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,639
Lord Valens.

83
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,639
There's no need for that.

84
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:03,799
Osman won't have a future.

85
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:07,879
Now, Bursa is under my command.

86
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:12,879
I'll bury him in to
the lands he was born.

87
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:19,959
With or without Nayman.

88
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:42,159
It's unlike the ones we've seen before.

89
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:45,279
I think those who are Lords
become commanders here, Bey.

90
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:48,759
No. They are trained
to kill all the soldiers.

91
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:51,599
Their armor is reinforced
from Constantinople.

92
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:54,439
With our current order, the
conquest is impossible.

93
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,759
There is system in their army, Bey.

94
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:07,959
Bursa is like that. What about the Lord?
Do you know anything about him?

95
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,319
We couldn't see the Lord, my Bey.

96
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:17,159
But it seems these plans are his.

97
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:22,079
He also strengthens the walls.
Catapults will not be enough.

98
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:30,719
Lord Valens is not only a commander.

99
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:35,879
He is a skillful commander
raised by Byzantium.

100
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:41,519
But Bursa is not just a city,

101
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:44,079
It has a regular army.

102
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:47,599
What troubles me...

103
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:53,039
İs being stuck between two enemies.

104
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,119
Baysungur.

105
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:04,039
Sons.

106
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:07,599
Now, you deserve a water.

107
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:18,319
There's news from the scouts, Bey.

108
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,719
Nayman has gone to the Lord of Bursa.

109
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:25,519
Really?

110
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,319
Gather the council at once!

111
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:35,999
Come on, sons.

112
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:51,319
What do you mean the mine is changed?
What were you doing?

113
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:57,239
We didn't understand how it happened.
It appeared when the mines cooled down.

114
00:14:58,640 --> 00:15:01,199
This is not the good we brought.

115
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:07,039
Is this how you do your work?
Don't you check it?

116
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:11,119
- What is this?
- You are right, Bala Hatun.

117
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:17,759
Immediately call the person who received
this mine and the person who delivered it.

118
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:21,119
All will be questioned. This
will be solved.

119
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:26,039
Malhun. Bala.
Osman Bey is gathering the council.

120
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,919
Those Alps will be here until we come
back.

121
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:43,999
Did Nayman receive
that note, Celali? Are you sure?

122
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:47,119
Why is there still no news?

123
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:52,279
Our soldiers took it to him, Mother
Sultan.

124
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:05,679
Why did that Nayman attack me?

125
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:08,599
There is something odd in this.

126
00:16:09,040 --> 00:16:13,199
Mother Sultan, forgive me but...

127
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:18,279
When blind people start seeing, the
first thing they get rid of is their stick.

128
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:24,079
Isn't it Nayman?
What is there to be surprised?

129
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:28,559
Apparently, he sacrificed you
after he gathered...

130
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:32,079
so many Beys behind him.

131
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:35,039
If he wanted to kill me...

132
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:38,719
he would find another
way for sure, Bayindir.

133
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:41,199
No...

134
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:48,919
You always know the best, my
Hadrat Mother Sultan.

135
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:56,679
Bayindir...

136
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:00,919
Go and check the forest..

137
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:05,637
where they attacked us.
See what happened there.

138
00:17:08,598 --> 00:17:11,358
Yes, my Mother Sultan.

139
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,396
Celali...

140
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:37,319
Bayindir talks too much.

141
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:41,359
Ever since we left Konya, he
keeps saying...

142
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:44,999
"Nayman will kill us."

143
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:49,079
He is after something again.

144
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:54,479
- Send a man after him.
- Yes, my Sultan.

145
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,359
Stop.

146
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:59,999
And call Bengi Hatun.

147
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:05,039
Let's ask her if she has done
her duties.

148
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:25,919
Welcome, Commander Nayman.
The Lord is waiting for you.

149
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:30,879
Why isn't Bursa's Lord welcoming us?

150
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:34,639
Our dear Lord welcomes the ones
superior to him at the door.

151
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:37,959
Such thing has not been
done yet, Commander Nayman.

152
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:44,359
When your Lord knows me,
he will kiss my feet.

153
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:46,519
Helper...

154
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:51,679
- Take me to your Lord.
- Follow me.

155
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:57,999
We hurt Nayman greatly.

156
00:18:58,280 --> 00:19:01,879
He can't even use his seal now.

157
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:08,079
This is the headquarter of Nayman.

158
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:11,679
With Beys' help...

159
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:16,879
we drew a bow here and stopped
his connection with North.

160
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:21,519
Therefore, he won't be able to
send a messenger there.

161
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:25,959
Nayman is stuck here.

162
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:29,759
Now, he will try to find
another way out.

163
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:33,279
He must have gone crazy, my Bey.

164
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,639
Uraz Bey.

165
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:42,439
Tell me what enemies do
when they go crazy.

166
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:45,839
They attack with all their power, my Bey.

167
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:48,759
Do you think Nayman will attack
with all his power?

168
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:56,239
If he was going to attack, we would know
his move by now.

169
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:03,439
What really worries us...

170
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:06,919
is the silence of the enemy.

171
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:11,679
Let's break the silence with the
sound of our swords, my Bey.

172
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:15,839
If he is silent, let's attack. Let's
not give an opportunity to him.

173
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:19,929
Alps want revenge.

174
00:20:20,044 --> 00:20:23,184
Tell them to attack, they'll
attack, tell them to die, they will die!

175
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:24,789
Let's attack his headquarters!

176
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:30,039
Since Alps are asking for war, let's
attack them like wolves attack sheep.

177
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:33,719
- Didn't you gather the council for the war?
- Beys...

178
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:37,879
We need not only brave
men walking to death...

179
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:41,079
not only speaking men..

180
00:20:41,520 --> 00:20:45,359
but also brave men
making the right moves.

181
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:52,639
Now tell me... Do you have an
intelligence to say these things?

182
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,839
Do you know the moves of Nayman?

183
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:59,519
- My Bey, we...
- Beys...

184
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,919
Nayman is stuck there.

185
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:09,839
But why didn't he attack?

186
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:13,479
Tell me, why didn't he?

187
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,879
Because Nayman has
another goal.

188
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:24,159
You are telling me to ride our horses
to death without knowing his goal.

189
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:29,279
Nayman went to Bursa's Lord
to ask for an alliance.

190
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:34,650
While we want to corner him between us and North...

191
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:37,180
he wants to corner us
between him and West.

192
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,319
Beys...

193
00:21:40,760 --> 00:21:43,159
It is easy to die on a bad day.

194
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:46,679
But we will make smart moves.

195
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:50,759
We will live, and we will win.

196
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,559
You want a war.

197
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:56,359
* /

198
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:58,759
I will give that war to you.

199
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:01,519
But not now.

200
00:22:05,320 --> 00:22:08,319
Now let's talk about why I
gathered the council.

201
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:11,079
Nayman...

202
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:13,999
went to Bursa's Lord.

203
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:19,719
We heard this from Orhan, if
Nayman and Lord agree...

204
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:24,359
let alone victory, our
existence will be in danger, Beys.

205
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:30,519
This Lord was commanding the navy
in the war between Byzantium and Venice.

206
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:33,919
He quelled many riots in west.

207
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:37,679
He won many wars.

208
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:40,959
It's not a coincidence that
they gave Bursa to him.

209
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:45,519
It’s not a coincidence that
Nayman went to him.

210
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:50,639
So, you are saying that the Lord is a
talented Commander, my Bey.

211
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:55,399
If he joins Nayman's evil
army, it won't be good for us.

212
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:06,279
Their soldiers and our Beys want war.

213
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:11,039
But Nayman is trying to build
an alliance with all his power.

214
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:14,719
What are we going to do?
What will be our move?

215
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:19,359
- How many slaves do we have?
- 12, my Bey.

216
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:24,279
- Cerkutay!
- My Bey.

217
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:36,479
So, you came here to
ask for my help, Nayman.

218
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:43,399
You will give food, water
and horses to my army.

219
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:49,759
You will give catapult
masters under my command.

220
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:54,519
And in return, you will
get so many things.

221
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:04,799
I will destroy Osman and build
an order in Konya and leave.

222
00:24:07,080 --> 00:24:11,719
Or else, you will get hurt badly, Lord.

223
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:16,999
Do not compare me..

224
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:20,599
to that shepherd Osman.

225
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,039
That would be a big mistake.

226
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,919
Don't trust your walls, Lord.

227
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:36,839
Once you leave here, an arrow may...

228
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:39,519
pierce your throat.

229
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:44,039
But...

230
00:24:45,120 --> 00:24:47,679
your enemy is Osman.

231
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:50,639
I am not your enemy.

232
00:24:51,390 --> 00:24:53,909
The only reason of your bravery...

233
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:58,199
is the seal of Genghis.

234
00:24:59,320 --> 00:25:03,399
I am the impassable
castle of Byzantium!

235
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:19,319
We've been fighting with
barbarians like you for centuries!

236
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:24,999
I can kill you here, Nayman.

237
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:34,759
But... some of the things
you said were right.

238
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:40,239
True. Osman is our
common enemy.

239
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:45,719
Working with a
barbarian like you...

240
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:49,079
will disturb me..

241
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:55,559
I will think about what you said.

242
00:25:56,840 --> 00:26:01,359
You are doing the right thing
for both of us, Lord.

243
00:26:12,600 --> 00:26:16,679
We could cut him into pieces with
a command of yours, my Lord.

244
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:19,519
Why did you...---

245
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:26,839
Nayman did not threaten us.

246
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:29,599
He is mad at Osman.

247
00:26:30,640 --> 00:26:35,439
Why would we kill him when
we could use his anger, Leo?

248
00:26:39,320 --> 00:26:42,239
Nayman will be my sword.

249
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:48,119
Cerkutay, the plan is going
to start with you.

250
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:51,719
You'll shave your beard
and paint your eyes.

251
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:55,239
You will bring Mongolian
Cerkutay back.

252
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:59,839
Your command, my Bey.

253
00:27:03,040 --> 00:27:07,159
Turgut Bey.
After Cerkutay finishes his preparations,

254
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:09,359
he'll go among the prisoners.

255
00:27:09,520 --> 00:27:13,079
And you'll take the caravan
where Mongolians are.

256
00:27:13,720 --> 00:27:16,239
You'll lead the caravan.

257
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:20,559
When they attack the caravan, you'll
release the prisoners and come back.

258
00:27:20,800 --> 00:27:23,599
- Your command.
- Cerkutay.

259
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:26,199
You'll find out...

260
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:29,559
what Nayman is doing
and what he's planning.

261
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:32,599
Your command, my Bey.

262
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:35,719
Beys.

263
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:39,399
You'll train the rest of the Alps.

264
00:27:39,520 --> 00:27:42,559
You'll train an equip everyone
who can hold a sword.

265
00:27:42,680 --> 00:27:45,959
From blacksmith to teachers.
Everyone.

266
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:50,999
What would a teacher do in
a battle, my Bey?

267
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:56,119
Surely, teachers will have
some difficulty at first.

268
00:27:56,520 --> 00:28:00,439
But when they're trained
and assigned in the army,

269
00:28:00,560 --> 00:28:03,999
they will be no different from the Alps.

270
00:28:10,840 --> 00:28:13,319
I am going to march to Bursa.

271
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:25,399
If Nayman seeks an alliance,

272
00:28:26,080 --> 00:28:29,559
then, I will ruin his alliance.

273
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:36,039
Come on. Everyone go
to their duties now.

274
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:50,759
Hatuns.

275
00:28:51,360 --> 00:28:53,839
Tell me what the coin matter is.

276
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:58,399
They changed the mines, my Bey.

277
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:10,399
Well, Osman..

278
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:14,239
How could you even think
you could coin money?

279
00:29:15,760 --> 00:29:17,559
He will learn...

280
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:22,919
that he can't move in these
lands without my permission...

281
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:25,399
and my knowledge.

282
00:29:28,080 --> 00:29:30,159
I won't let him.

283
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:34,319
Well done, Bengi Hatun.

284
00:29:34,800 --> 00:29:37,599
You'll be rewarded for
your work.

285
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:41,599
Thanks, Mother Sultan.
Thanks to your help.

286
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:45,799
Hatuns must be investigating the matter now.

287
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:48,559
Let them investigate.

288
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:51,719
They can't find anything.

289
00:29:52,480 --> 00:29:55,919
The soldiers who helped you have
already been sent to Konya.

290
00:29:57,080 --> 00:29:58,919
The rest is up to you.

291
00:29:59,880 --> 00:30:03,239
I hid the real silver in the
tribe. Nobody can find it.

292
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:06,639
There's something bothering my mind.

293
00:30:08,040 --> 00:30:10,039
But I will figure it out.

294
00:30:17,800 --> 00:30:21,039
What is bothering you,, Bengi?

295
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:24,239
Esma.

296
00:30:24,760 --> 00:30:28,479
She was in the tribe when I arrived.
She saw nothing.

297
00:30:29,080 --> 00:30:31,399
But it bothered me.

298
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:34,519
I've sent my Alps to follow her.

299
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:37,719
You can't trust your luck, Bengi.

300
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:41,519
Don't let mercy
make you fail.

301
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:47,919
Intimidate her well.

302
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:53,319
- If you say you can't do it...
- I can.

303
00:30:56,120 --> 00:30:58,079
I can do it.

304
00:31:29,280 --> 00:31:30,769
Sit down.

305
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:33,319
Sit down here.

306
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:50,399
Attention!

307
00:32:07,280 --> 00:32:10,199
My Bey, have a safe travel.

308
00:32:10,840 --> 00:32:12,919
Don't be worrying about here.

309
00:32:13,120 --> 00:32:16,759
We will solve the
coin matter, Inshallah.

310
00:32:20,640 --> 00:32:22,279
We'll find the troublemaker.

311
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:26,319
I know, Hatuns.
May Allah protect you. Thanks.

312
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:28,439
- Come on.
- Come on.

313
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:32,959
What's the situation?

314
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:37,719
We're ready.
We can go when you want.

315
00:32:38,280 --> 00:32:40,199
Thanks.

316
00:32:40,800 --> 00:32:43,039
What's the situation?

317
00:32:44,080 --> 00:32:45,119
My Bey.

318
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:49,359
The goods loaded in the
caravan going to the Lord of Bursa.

319
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:50,839
Good.

320
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:54,839
The gifts for the Lord have been loaded
in a special wagon, my Bey.

321
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:57,119
Thanks, Konur.

322
00:32:58,080 --> 00:33:01,879
Turgut, when the caravan arrives, you'll
make the Alps practice.

323
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:03,599
Yes.

324
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:06,479
Come on. Everyone
get back to work.

325
00:33:08,280 --> 00:33:10,719
Look, ignoble Mongolian!

326
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:14,199
Perhaps, this is the last time you
see this mansion!

327
00:33:20,480 --> 00:33:22,439
Time to go, Alps.

328
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:25,839
Get up! Get up!

329
00:33:26,600 --> 00:33:27,839
Get up!

330
00:33:47,240 --> 00:33:49,639
Let's go.

331
00:34:10,400 --> 00:34:12,839
Come back to me quickly.

332
00:34:13,520 --> 00:34:14,918
Inshallah.

333
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:30,279
How do I look?

334
00:34:35,159 --> 00:34:37,159
- Cerkutay.
- Yes?

335
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:39,839
Why do you look like this?

336
00:34:40,040 --> 00:34:42,119
I'm going on a mission, Ülgen.

337
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:47,958
But there is something...

338
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:51,559
I need to know before I go.

339
00:34:54,040 --> 00:34:55,918
Well...

340
00:34:56,199 --> 00:34:58,599
I told you something.

341
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:01,399
Remember it?

342
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:05,119
Yes, I do.

343
00:35:05,360 --> 00:35:08,999
Well, I need to know that.

344
00:35:10,040 --> 00:35:11,359
Oh.

345
00:35:15,080 --> 00:35:18,039
Cerkutay.
Well...

346
00:35:21,560 --> 00:35:23,719
I love you too.

347
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:31,559
- Then...
- But...

348
00:35:32,280 --> 00:35:34,639
- But?
- My mother.

349
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:36,639
The dark midwife.

350
00:35:36,840 --> 00:35:39,399
She will never let me marry you.

351
00:35:39,960 --> 00:35:41,639
Oh my...

352
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:45,919
Help! Mongolians
attacked the house!

353
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:48,439
Hey, stop!
Stop.

354
00:35:48,600 --> 00:35:51,559
Mother, please stop!
He's Cerkutay.

355
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:54,239
It's me.
Cerkutay.

356
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:58,159
It's really you.

357
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:01,119
Mad man!

358
00:36:01,880 --> 00:36:03,719
What is this?

359
00:36:05,120 --> 00:36:09,239
I'm going for a mission.
Let me kiss your hand.

360
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:11,879
Well.

361
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:16,119
You're going into the
nest of the enemy, huh?

362
00:36:17,640 --> 00:36:21,239
Mashallah!
Mad man!

363
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:25,159
You are crazy but you're courageous!

364
00:36:26,720 --> 00:36:31,639
Well, I contributed
to your mission!

365
00:36:31,760 --> 00:36:34,559
Yes, you cracked my head
open again.

366
00:36:39,440 --> 00:36:44,039
Still...
What are you doing with my daughter?

367
00:36:45,320 --> 00:36:46,719
Nothing, mother.

368
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:47,999
- Mother.
- Yes.

369
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:50,319
Come. Let me explain.

370
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:55,799
Well, I worked as a spy
for a really long time.

371
00:36:56,440 --> 00:37:00,039
And to ask my
opinion, Cerkutay said...

372
00:37:00,080 --> 00:37:03,759
"Ülgen... Sister Ülgen", he said.

373
00:37:04,080 --> 00:37:06,239
- Well...
- Oh.

374
00:37:09,520 --> 00:37:11,359
Ülgen!

375
00:37:12,680 --> 00:37:14,519
Ülgen!

376
00:37:15,080 --> 00:37:17,959
Ülgen Hatun, we have much work to do.

377
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:23,799
I'm coming, mother.
I'm coming.

378
00:37:30,440 --> 00:37:35,219
Malhun Hatun, we investigated but
couldn't find the Alps who received the wagon.

379
00:37:35,240 --> 00:37:38,559
What do you mean?
You don't know them at all?

380
00:37:38,640 --> 00:37:41,239
No. We saw them for
the first time there.

381
00:37:42,760 --> 00:37:48,199
You delivered the mines to the men who
you saw for the first time, huh?

382
00:37:50,480 --> 00:37:52,279
And you received
them?

383
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:01,459
So... Why didn't you check at all
when you received the mines?

384
00:38:01,520 --> 00:38:04,979
We checked but they can't be
distinguished before melting.

385
00:38:05,040 --> 00:38:08,559
Whoever did this, it must be someone
who knows the mines well.

386
00:38:11,680 --> 00:38:13,479
Ismihan.

387
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:16,479
If you are behind this...

388
00:38:17,800 --> 00:38:20,679
Someone must be telling
Ismihan what we are doing.

389
00:38:20,880 --> 00:38:22,959
I have somebody in my mind, but...

390
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:25,759
We'll figure it out.

391
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:30,639
Find out where this mine
is mined and where this is coming from.

392
00:38:30,840 --> 00:38:34,799
When we find the source,
we will find who did it.

393
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:37,849
Send Alps all around.

394
00:38:37,990 --> 00:38:41,939
Obviously, the one who received the mines
changed them with the bad ones on the way.

395
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:45,839
Find those Alps! They must
have left a trace behind.

396
00:38:46,840 --> 00:38:50,359
Until we find out who did this, none
of us will sleep!

397
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:09,119
Sons.

398
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:11,639
The road splits up here.

399
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:16,159
One way leads to Bursa
and the other one leads to Iznik.

400
00:39:18,440 --> 00:39:20,559
I don't see separate ways, my Bey.

401
00:39:20,640 --> 00:39:24,879
Both are the ways leading us to the
conquests and to our new lands.

402
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:31,879
But today you were saying
it was impossible, son.

403
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:35,919
The impossible only
takes some time, my Bey.

404
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:42,399
When we work together, we
can take any land.

405
00:39:43,200 --> 00:39:45,039
Yes.

406
00:39:47,240 --> 00:39:51,679
Tell me how it's going to be.
I'm listening to you.

407
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:56,559
My Bey, Bursa is ten
times as big as Inegol.

408
00:39:57,440 --> 00:40:01,559
It’s not a castle but a city.

409
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:07,359
We need a regular army to conquer Bursa.

410
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:10,599
My brother and I were discussing this.

411
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:14,199
Our Alps should only engage in fighting.

412
00:40:15,080 --> 00:40:17,479
They should be paid by the state.

413
00:40:18,920 --> 00:40:20,839
But, sons...

414
00:40:22,040 --> 00:40:25,519
You're talking about something impossible
which will take time.

415
00:40:27,240 --> 00:40:30,879
Forcing tribe people to
do this is really hard.

416
00:40:34,080 --> 00:40:36,599
We have to if we want Bursa, my Bey.

417
00:40:37,800 --> 00:40:41,159
We need such an army to
besiege it from all directions.

418
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:46,119
That's right, sons. But...

419
00:40:46,680 --> 00:40:49,359
We need to bring a new order for people.

420
00:40:49,600 --> 00:40:53,479
We need to increase the taxes.
Now, tell me...

421
00:40:54,040 --> 00:40:56,719
How are you going to feed the Alps?

422
00:40:57,160 --> 00:41:00,639
When we get rid of the enemy
outside and the traitor inside,

423
00:41:00,720 --> 00:41:03,559
we'll be powerful enough
to feed them, my Bey.

424
00:41:04,520 --> 00:41:08,279
Thanks, sons.

425
00:41:09,680 --> 00:41:13,199
This is your new duty.

426
00:41:14,560 --> 00:41:17,959
- Your command, my Bey.
- Your command, my Bey.

427
00:41:18,680 --> 00:41:22,119
Come on! Our horses
have rested enough.

428
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:25,479
Us too.

429
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:30,199
We can't rest during the conquest.
We should arrive before the caravan.

430
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:32,599
Let's go, sons.

431
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:36,679
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

432
00:41:43,040 --> 00:41:45,639
Mother Sultan.
Nayman...

433
00:41:46,600 --> 00:41:48,959
Ismihan!

434
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:55,439
What are you up to?

435
00:41:58,360 --> 00:42:00,479
Why didn't you attend the council?

436
00:42:01,240 --> 00:42:04,399
You attempted to kill me on the
way to the council!

437
00:42:05,240 --> 00:42:08,679
Why? You got the seal first.

438
00:42:09,280 --> 00:42:12,439
Then you wanted to get rid of me.

439
00:42:14,440 --> 00:42:16,879
And now are you even questioning me?

440
00:42:19,920 --> 00:42:22,359
If I had attempted to kill you,

441
00:42:22,920 --> 00:42:25,999
you wouldn't be here now, Mother Sultan.

442
00:42:27,600 --> 00:42:31,079
The arrow I shoot
always hits the target.

443
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:35,999
If wanted to kill you...

444
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:39,759
...would I come
here only with one soldier?

445
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:48,799
There is a game going on.

446
00:42:49,880 --> 00:42:53,719
Obviously, it's not us who made the game.

447
00:43:08,240 --> 00:43:09,799
Osman.

448
00:43:41,080 --> 00:43:43,359
Your swords, Osman Bey.

449
00:43:48,200 --> 00:43:50,599
Come on, sons.

450
00:44:00,560 --> 00:44:02,679
You'll wait, Osman Bey.

451
00:44:19,320 --> 00:44:21,599
Come over here.

452
00:44:26,840 --> 00:44:30,719
Is that so? Alright.

453
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:38,599
Goodbye, Tradesman Tasinis.

454
00:44:42,480 --> 00:44:44,759
Is it time, father?

455
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:05,199
We'll wait, sons.

456
00:45:06,920 --> 00:45:08,839
We'll wait.

457
00:45:22,080 --> 00:45:24,079
Goodbye, Commander Saneri.

458
00:45:28,880 --> 00:45:31,029
You'll wait longer, Osman Bey.

459
00:45:31,050 --> 00:45:33,729
Mighty Lord has more precious guests.

460
00:45:33,780 --> 00:45:35,419
Is that so?

461
00:45:38,320 --> 00:45:40,599
Dear Dermos, welcome.

462
00:45:40,880 --> 00:45:42,759
Mighty Lord is waiting for you.

463
00:45:59,880 --> 00:46:01,199
My sons.

464
00:46:01,360 --> 00:46:05,279
Every leader must think about
his people first.

465
00:46:05,760 --> 00:46:08,279
Let's wait for a while longer.

466
00:46:09,080 --> 00:46:11,239
What is the purpose
of the Lord, father?

467
00:46:11,440 --> 00:46:13,999
He thinks he
is punishing us, son.

468
00:46:15,520 --> 00:46:19,039
We know our place, my Bey.
But this is too much.

469
00:46:19,840 --> 00:46:21,999
I'll eventually make him pay for this.

470
00:46:22,520 --> 00:46:24,279
Wait a second, son.

471
00:46:34,920 --> 00:46:36,239
Hurry up!

472
00:46:36,520 --> 00:46:39,679
Mighty Lord does not like to wait
for the food.

473
00:47:09,880 --> 00:47:12,199
Yes, Osman Bey?

474
00:47:13,640 --> 00:47:15,919
Come on, sons.

475
00:47:55,040 --> 00:47:58,519
The lamb I'm eating...

476
00:48:00,520 --> 00:48:02,399
is pretty delicious.

477
00:48:04,160 --> 00:48:08,479
What is a shepherd who cannot do better
than to serve me in my kitchen...

478
00:48:09,880 --> 00:48:12,119
doing in my presence?

479
00:48:19,600 --> 00:48:21,839
I heard that you met Nayman.

480
00:48:23,840 --> 00:48:25,919
That's why I'm here.

481
00:48:32,040 --> 00:48:37,149
Are you questioning me just because I
meet your enemy?

482
00:48:38,080 --> 00:48:40,759
I'm not going to question you.

483
00:48:45,880 --> 00:48:47,479
However...

484
00:48:48,840 --> 00:48:52,519
you will tell me whether you
made a deal with Nayman or not.

485
00:48:55,760 --> 00:48:58,999
See? You've started questioning.

486
00:49:04,120 --> 00:49:06,279
Why are your kids here with you?

487
00:49:10,640 --> 00:49:12,799
Do you think I will feel pity for you...

488
00:49:13,200 --> 00:49:16,719
and not kill you
while they are here?

489
00:49:21,560 --> 00:49:23,759
I heard your name.

490
00:49:26,840 --> 00:49:31,639
Since I heard that you won so
many battles,

491
00:49:32,400 --> 00:49:35,479
I wanted my kids to meet you as well.

492
00:49:38,160 --> 00:49:40,679
You know everything, Osman.

493
00:49:42,040 --> 00:49:44,279
You also know that you will be ruined...

494
00:49:44,840 --> 00:49:47,559
when I unite with Nayman.

495
00:49:51,480 --> 00:49:54,919
Yes, tell me. What do you want?

496
00:49:57,640 --> 00:49:59,639
You...

497
00:50:00,600 --> 00:50:03,319
you know so little, Lord Valens.

498
00:50:04,280 --> 00:50:06,199
So little.

499
00:50:07,480 --> 00:50:11,279
Open them.
I said open them.

500
00:50:27,640 --> 00:50:32,359
Do you think Nayman will
unite with you only for me?

501
00:50:34,480 --> 00:50:38,119
You didn't care about how
small you are and you hit him well.

502
00:50:39,960 --> 00:50:41,919
You made him dependent on me.

503
00:50:43,520 --> 00:50:45,239
Just like you.

504
00:50:46,800 --> 00:50:50,279
Of course it will be hard
for us if you unite together.

505
00:50:51,320 --> 00:50:54,679
But Nayman's actual purpose...

506
00:50:56,120 --> 00:50:59,159
is to lead
you into a big war.

507
00:51:01,640 --> 00:51:03,959
Nayman's problem is with Ghazan Khan,

508
00:51:04,480 --> 00:51:07,999
If you're going to be friends
with Nayman,

509
00:51:09,680 --> 00:51:12,439
then you are going to be
the enemy of Ghazan Khan.

510
00:51:13,280 --> 00:51:15,639
This has nothing to do with me.

511
00:51:16,120 --> 00:51:19,559
This is about Ghazan Khan.

512
00:51:24,040 --> 00:51:28,159
If you are going to oppose
the great Ilkhanids,

513
00:51:29,520 --> 00:51:31,679
then, it's up to you to decide.

514
00:51:32,440 --> 00:51:35,039
You can't even imagine the things...

515
00:51:35,960 --> 00:51:38,359
I'll be opposing, Osman.

516
00:51:40,120 --> 00:51:41,999
Let alone Ghazan Khan...

517
00:51:42,520 --> 00:51:47,039
even if Genghis revives, he will
end up dead in front of my walls.

518
00:51:55,520 --> 00:51:57,799
So Osman dispersed your army as well?

519
00:51:59,360 --> 00:52:02,119
Osman wants me to be alone.

520
00:52:03,280 --> 00:52:07,439
We will become enemies and
he will take advantage of it.

521
00:52:08,440 --> 00:52:10,199
But how?

522
00:52:10,720 --> 00:52:13,719
It is impossible for Osman to
know our cooperation.

523
00:52:14,920 --> 00:52:18,039
They say walls have ears, Mother Sultan.

524
00:52:18,360 --> 00:52:21,959
It seems Osman rules over those ears.

525
00:52:23,800 --> 00:52:25,479
Osman.

526
00:52:26,520 --> 00:52:29,079
You want to play games, right?

527
00:52:29,720 --> 00:52:31,599
Let’s play, then.

528
00:52:32,040 --> 00:52:34,439
No more games, Mother Sultan.

529
00:52:34,800 --> 00:52:39,359
The more Osman tries to leave me
alone, the more I get stronger.

530
00:52:46,200 --> 00:52:49,439
Lord of Bursa will obey me.

531
00:52:49,960 --> 00:52:53,079
I will have a new ally.

532
00:52:54,640 --> 00:52:56,439
How did you do this, Nayman?

533
00:52:57,400 --> 00:53:01,479
You are settled in Konya, he is in Bursa.

534
00:53:01,920 --> 00:53:05,719
He knows that he will be destroyed
if he doesn't unite with me.

535
00:53:06,840 --> 00:53:07,799
Good.

536
00:53:08,640 --> 00:53:10,879
Your alliance...

537
00:53:11,320 --> 00:53:13,399
is my alliance.

538
00:53:14,040 --> 00:53:17,079
I didn't just wait while you
were looking for allies.

539
00:53:17,160 --> 00:53:20,679
I started the move that will ruin
Osman from the inside.

540
00:53:23,080 --> 00:53:26,159
You, from the outside and I, from the inside...

541
00:53:26,920 --> 00:53:29,239
we will destroy Osman.

542
00:53:29,520 --> 00:53:33,839
I can't wait to cut
Osman's head, Mother Sultan.

543
00:53:34,840 --> 00:53:37,159
Don't forget that.

544
00:53:45,560 --> 00:53:47,279
How can Osman...

545
00:53:48,120 --> 00:53:52,479
know our steps beforehand?

546
00:53:56,760 --> 00:53:58,479
Summon...

547
00:53:59,560 --> 00:54:02,439
Bayindir here.

548
00:54:03,520 --> 00:54:05,959
Yes, Mother Sultan.

549
00:54:08,280 --> 00:54:10,039
Bayindir.

550
00:54:10,400 --> 00:54:12,999
If you betray me...

551
00:54:13,360 --> 00:54:15,199
I'll bury your dead body...

552
00:54:16,160 --> 00:54:20,479
all around these lands.

553
00:54:40,600 --> 00:54:42,279
Do you think they take the bait?

554
00:54:42,480 --> 00:54:45,759
We will see, brother.
We will see.

555
00:54:45,800 --> 00:54:47,959
They can get into the
cage at any moment.

556
00:54:47,960 --> 00:54:51,839
Still, keep your eyes open.
They might come out of anywhere.

557
00:54:51,880 --> 00:54:55,959
If Osman Bey didn't order otherwise, I
would crush all those infidels.

558
00:54:56,160 --> 00:55:01,239
Anyway, the food of the infidels is sword
and the place they will go is hell.

559
00:55:12,360 --> 00:55:15,519
Be careful, Alps!

560
00:55:20,520 --> 00:55:22,399
Let the game begin.

561
00:56:16,040 --> 00:56:19,999
There are too many of them, Alps!
We will retreat, come on!

562
00:56:33,720 --> 00:56:35,559
Save us.

563
00:56:37,000 --> 00:56:39,679
You are incompetent.

564
00:56:39,680 --> 00:56:43,759
But you will live and
you will serve Nayman.

565
00:56:44,520 --> 00:56:48,439
Untie them! Then, take them to
the headquarters, come on!

566
00:57:15,800 --> 00:57:19,399
A shepherd with fewer soldiers
than the number of his sheep,

567
00:57:20,120 --> 00:57:21,919
is trying to teach me politics.

568
00:57:24,120 --> 00:57:26,959
He is talking about a big war.

569
00:57:31,560 --> 00:57:33,959
Who do you think you are, Osman?

570
00:57:35,840 --> 00:57:38,199
I'm the one who can
see what you can't...

571
00:57:39,880 --> 00:57:42,199
and knows what you don't know.

572
00:57:44,400 --> 00:57:48,319
Ghazan Khan is talking to
the Altın Orda state...

573
00:57:49,400 --> 00:57:53,479
and states never show
mercy to the rebels.

574
00:57:54,960 --> 00:57:57,799
If you collaborate with a rebel...

575
00:57:59,080 --> 00:58:01,479
you will be ruined.

576
00:58:05,040 --> 00:58:07,119
This is a warning for you.

577
00:58:08,360 --> 00:58:10,799
Don't side with Nayman,

578
00:58:11,520 --> 00:58:12,999
and stop this bloodshed.

579
00:58:13,320 --> 00:58:16,839
Or, Byzantium army...

580
00:58:17,480 --> 00:58:19,599
will unite with Nayman...

581
00:58:19,960 --> 00:58:23,319
and they will destroy Ghazan and you.

582
00:58:25,720 --> 00:58:29,959
I will rule all the lands with
its old glory.

583
00:58:33,200 --> 00:58:36,079
The seal that Nayman has
will be the end of all of us.

584
00:58:44,040 --> 00:58:47,519
Mighty Lord, the messengers of
Commander Nayman are here.

585
00:59:09,200 --> 00:59:11,439
You can leave, Osman.

586
00:59:12,800 --> 00:59:15,799
Today, the destiny of you is up to me.

587
00:59:21,120 --> 00:59:23,919
For a shepherd that
you didn't even let inside...

588
00:59:25,600 --> 00:59:28,199
you lined up archers here.

589
00:59:39,720 --> 00:59:42,119
Tell them to be comfortable.

590
01:00:04,240 --> 01:00:07,679
Great Commander Nayman is
waiting to hear from you, Lord.

591
01:00:12,520 --> 01:00:16,719
How many soldiers are there in
Nayman's army, messenger?

592
01:00:17,080 --> 01:00:21,079
Thousands of soldiers are ready to
shed blood for him.

593
01:00:23,800 --> 01:00:27,839
What about Ghazan Khan's army?

594
01:00:30,600 --> 01:00:32,599
Ilkhanid army...

595
01:00:33,560 --> 01:00:36,079
has more than thousands of men.

596
01:00:39,920 --> 01:00:42,119
Being a messenger is a tough task.

597
01:00:44,040 --> 01:00:46,119
Special ones are chosen.

598
01:00:47,160 --> 01:00:49,199
Answer me, Messenger.

599
01:00:53,000 --> 01:00:56,039
Would the seal Nayman has...

600
01:00:59,320 --> 01:01:02,559
be enough to resist...

601
01:01:11,440 --> 01:01:13,799
when Ilkhanids and Altın Orda unite?

602
01:01:13,920 --> 01:01:17,679
I'm here to receive answer, I'm
not here to answer.

603
01:01:26,000 --> 01:01:28,079
You just answered.

604
01:01:41,200 --> 01:01:42,959
And this is my answer.

605
01:01:46,920 --> 01:01:49,879
Is this the right decision, Mighty Lord?

606
01:01:51,200 --> 01:01:55,679
Cut heads are better than
confused heads, Leo.

607
01:01:59,600 --> 01:02:03,879
I will not oppose Ghazan Khan
just to destroy Osman.

608
01:02:06,400 --> 01:02:08,639
When the time comes...

609
01:02:09,040 --> 01:02:11,559
I'll be the one who puts an
end to the war.

610
01:02:24,240 --> 01:02:26,439
Malhun Hatun, may I come in?

611
01:02:26,560 --> 01:02:28,599
Come in, Esma.

612
01:02:39,640 --> 01:02:41,879
What happened, Esma?

613
01:02:43,480 --> 01:02:44,919
Are you crying?

614
01:02:45,520 --> 01:02:47,959
What happened?
Did someone do something?

615
01:02:49,840 --> 01:02:51,399
Not to me.

616
01:02:53,520 --> 01:02:57,279
But those who changed the mines
which we will make the coins with...

617
01:02:58,200 --> 01:02:59,399
they...

618
01:02:59,520 --> 01:03:03,559
What are you saying, Esma?
We've been looking for this since morning.

619
01:03:03,560 --> 01:03:05,359
Tell me what you know!

620
01:03:05,730 --> 01:03:09,369
I went to Kargun tribe as Ayse
Hatun had something to send.

621
01:03:10,480 --> 01:03:11,959
Bengi?

622
01:03:14,440 --> 01:03:17,159
Why didn't you say it before, Esma?

623
01:03:18,320 --> 01:03:20,839
I was afraid, I was so afraid.

624
01:03:21,880 --> 01:03:24,599
They changed the mines.

625
01:03:26,600 --> 01:03:29,759
I was afraid that Bengi Hatun
would take my sibling again.

626
01:03:33,680 --> 01:03:36,359
But I couldn't stop myself, Malhun Hatun.

627
01:03:36,760 --> 01:03:38,679
I couldn't.

628
01:03:39,520 --> 01:03:43,079
Bengi.

629
01:03:44,600 --> 01:03:47,319
Let's see what is
your excuse this time.

630
01:03:48,760 --> 01:03:52,039
I'll make your life hell!

631
01:03:55,600 --> 01:03:59,159
Malhun Hatun, please don't
say my name.

632
01:03:59,840 --> 01:04:03,959
She'll be even angrier at me when she
hears that you've heard it from me.

633
01:04:04,640 --> 01:04:06,519
I'm so afraid.

634
01:04:08,680 --> 01:04:12,359
I'm thinking about my sibling's life
more than mine.

635
01:04:13,720 --> 01:04:15,839
Get up, Esma.
Get up.

636
01:04:17,360 --> 01:04:21,019
You are under the protection
of Malhun Hatun.

637
01:04:33,760 --> 01:04:36,279
Here, take this.

638
01:04:39,120 --> 01:04:42,199
Don't be afraid to use it when needed.

639
01:04:42,480 --> 01:04:44,119
Be careful.

640
01:04:44,600 --> 01:04:48,919
Don't wander alone, don't ever
trust anyone.

641
01:04:54,800 --> 01:04:57,159
Thank you, Malhun Hatun.

642
01:04:59,400 --> 01:05:01,159
Thank you.

643
01:05:03,240 --> 01:05:05,639
We will be here for sure.

644
01:05:06,360 --> 01:05:08,039
But...

645
01:05:08,720 --> 01:05:11,159
they will be punished.

646
01:05:25,960 --> 01:05:27,319
Yenişehir is this way.

647
01:05:27,320 --> 01:05:29,119
Not to Yenişehir...

648
01:05:29,120 --> 01:05:32,399
we're going to the cave near Günova.

649
01:05:37,920 --> 01:05:39,159
My Bey.

650
01:05:39,560 --> 01:05:41,919
Warriors guard there.

651
01:05:41,920 --> 01:05:44,779
They’ll attack us when
we set foot there.

652
01:05:44,800 --> 01:05:48,109
The number of the warriors standing
guard is three times ours, my Bey.

653
01:05:48,200 --> 01:05:50,539
We can't get out without
loss if we go there.

654
01:05:50,760 --> 01:05:54,039
If you give us order, let's go
there from this road.

655
01:05:54,400 --> 01:05:56,679
The roads are safe and
they can't ambush.

656
01:05:56,680 --> 01:05:58,239
No.

657
01:05:59,200 --> 01:06:00,959
If we go that way, it
will take longer.

658
01:06:00,960 --> 01:06:02,639
We'll go this way.

659
01:06:02,640 --> 01:06:04,599
We won't obey them.

660
01:06:04,600 --> 01:06:07,119
We'll kill them.

661
01:06:07,600 --> 01:06:09,119
Now, listen to me well.

662
01:06:46,960 --> 01:06:47,679
Now!

663
01:06:48,120 --> 01:06:49,159
Allah is the Greatest!

664
01:06:49,440 --> 01:06:51,679
Allah is the Greatest!

665
01:07:14,200 --> 01:07:17,799
You know what to do, my sons.

666
01:09:02,960 --> 01:09:04,799
You're going to die...

667
01:09:05,200 --> 01:09:08,799
one by one.

668
01:09:11,078 --> 01:09:12,618
Alps.

669
01:09:18,439 --> 01:09:20,439
Let's not keep Sultan Mesut waiting.

670
01:09:20,600 --> 01:09:22,559
We're going to him now.

671
01:09:23,359 --> 01:09:25,158
Bring the horses.

672
01:09:39,160 --> 01:09:41,198
So, it's time for me to take
off the dervish cardigan...

673
01:09:41,560 --> 01:09:45,359
and wear the royal robes, Osman Bey.

674
01:09:46,600 --> 01:09:48,799
We will start a great war soon.

675
01:09:49,080 --> 01:09:53,999
But Konya still supports
Nayman, my Sultan.

676
01:09:55,480 --> 01:09:58,879
Supporting those who are
here to destroy these lands...

677
01:09:59,240 --> 01:10:01,159
is nothing but despair, Osman Bey.

678
01:10:02,600 --> 01:10:07,799
Back in the day, you came all the
way from Konya to my tribe...

679
01:10:09,000 --> 01:10:11,919
just to stop me from killing Geyhatu.

680
01:10:14,120 --> 01:10:16,919
That was only to avoid
more problems, Osman Bey.

681
01:10:17,600 --> 01:10:21,079
I was thinking that was the
way to keep the peace.

682
01:10:21,360 --> 01:10:23,599
That's what they're thinking now.

683
01:10:24,080 --> 01:10:28,999
They think Konya will be saved if
they work with Nayman.

684
01:10:29,840 --> 01:10:31,639
But this war is different than
any other.

685
01:10:33,200 --> 01:10:35,999
It's a war between right and wrong.

686
01:10:38,440 --> 01:10:42,959
He, who bows down to oppression, will
never be victorious.

687
01:10:46,520 --> 01:10:48,519
You're right, Osman Bey.

688
01:10:49,280 --> 01:10:52,799
I will keep your words in
mind when I sit on the throne.

689
01:10:54,200 --> 01:10:55,799
My Sultan...

690
01:10:56,280 --> 01:10:59,399
please don't forget about the promise
you made to support us.

691
01:10:59,800 --> 01:11:01,559
I won’t.

692
01:11:01,840 --> 01:11:06,359
Tell me what
our final move is going to be.

693
01:11:07,400 --> 01:11:09,639
We're going to do what
we always do.

694
01:11:09,920 --> 01:11:14,199
We will make our plans perfect
and attack the infidels.

695
01:11:20,800 --> 01:11:23,719
I swear, Mother Sultan!

696
01:11:24,120 --> 01:11:26,839
I would never betray you!

697
01:11:27,120 --> 01:11:29,679
Nayman's name was the first
one that I could think of...

698
01:11:29,840 --> 01:11:31,679
and that's why I said it.

699
01:11:31,840 --> 01:11:34,839
I wanted to be careful.

700
01:11:36,400 --> 01:11:40,959
You were only careful about Nayman, I
don't know why.

701
01:11:43,360 --> 01:11:45,879
You didn't even mention Osman.

702
01:11:46,480 --> 01:11:48,519
Mother Sultan..

703
01:11:48,640 --> 01:11:53,559
how am I supposed to know about that
demon Osman was making such a plan?

704
01:11:53,920 --> 01:11:56,919
Heathen Nayman or the demon Osman...

705
01:11:57,200 --> 01:11:58,879
They're both the same for me.

706
01:11:58,880 --> 01:12:01,399
I wish death for both!

707
01:12:01,520 --> 01:12:03,799
My only concern is...

708
01:12:04,600 --> 01:12:07,999
to protect your life!

709
01:12:08,000 --> 01:12:09,959
Bayindir...

710
01:12:11,800 --> 01:12:13,839
Even a single proof...

711
01:12:14,080 --> 01:12:18,759
will be enough for me
to feed you to dogs.

712
01:12:19,880 --> 01:12:21,959
If you betray me...

713
01:12:22,440 --> 01:12:25,879
your life will be really short.

714
01:12:26,120 --> 01:12:29,039
Mother Sultan...

715
01:12:29,640 --> 01:12:32,159
if want to feel good...

716
01:12:32,920 --> 01:12:35,599
you don't need proof.

717
01:12:36,320 --> 01:12:38,799
My life is yours to take!

718
01:12:39,200 --> 01:12:41,399
But..

719
01:12:41,560 --> 01:12:44,399
I'm only concerned for you.

720
01:12:44,800 --> 01:12:49,599
Osman clearly sent a traitor among us.

721
01:12:50,080 --> 01:12:53,359
That traitor can be here among us...

722
01:12:54,160 --> 01:12:56,919
but he can be next
to Nayman as well.

723
01:12:57,240 --> 01:12:59,039
How are we supposed to know?

724
01:12:59,480 --> 01:13:01,559
Are you saying that Osman placed...

725
01:13:01,800 --> 01:13:04,439
...a Turk spy inside in the Mongol base?

726
01:13:04,600 --> 01:13:06,119
No...

727
01:13:06,400 --> 01:13:08,719
..not a Turk.

728
01:13:09,480 --> 01:13:13,279
He might have placed a Mongolian spy there.

729
01:13:14,800 --> 01:13:18,639
You know, as well as I do, Mother Sultan...

730
01:13:19,560 --> 01:13:21,799
..that Nayman does not like me.

731
01:13:22,480 --> 01:13:25,399
But it is not important at all.

732
01:13:25,960 --> 01:13:30,879
Give me the order and I'll go into
that heathen Nayman's cave...

733
01:13:31,240 --> 01:13:34,239
..and take that spy out!

734
01:13:44,920 --> 01:13:48,959
I give you one last chance, Bayindir.

735
01:13:52,120 --> 01:13:54,439
Cerkutay will be inside the headquarters.

736
01:13:54,560 --> 01:13:57,799
And you will be the bridge between us.

737
01:13:58,160 --> 01:14:01,719
Get into the Nayman’s headquarters
one way or another.

738
01:14:01,840 --> 01:14:04,399
You'll be in touch with Cerkutay.

739
01:14:04,400 --> 01:14:07,559
And you will sustain the
connection between us.

740
01:14:08,400 --> 01:14:10,039
As you order, my Bey.

741
01:14:13,240 --> 01:14:15,959
NAYMAN'S BASE

742
01:14:16,480 --> 01:14:18,799
You! What is your profession?

743
01:14:18,800 --> 01:14:20,479
I shoot arrows well.

744
01:14:21,240 --> 01:14:23,359
-What about you?
-I'm a blacksmith.

745
01:14:23,360 --> 01:14:25,599
No one is a carver?

746
01:14:28,920 --> 01:14:32,039
You need a carpenter.

747
01:14:32,880 --> 01:14:35,319
Why do you need one?

748
01:14:40,200 --> 01:14:44,799
You! Answer my question.
You know woodcraft?

749
01:14:46,240 --> 01:14:49,159
There is lots of kinds of woods.

750
01:14:49,680 --> 01:14:51,999
If you want me to carve spoon.

751
01:14:53,480 --> 01:14:54,799
Then, I don't know.

752
01:14:55,200 --> 01:14:57,519
But if it is something big...

753
01:14:58,400 --> 01:15:01,479
Take him. Take him to the carvers.

754
01:15:01,600 --> 01:15:04,679
And take the others to the blacksmiths.

755
01:15:06,400 --> 01:15:07,679
Get up now.

756
01:15:08,840 --> 01:15:09,999
Come here.

757
01:15:25,480 --> 01:15:27,999
Speak, Tendu.

758
01:15:28,240 --> 01:15:32,639
The soldiers we sent to watch duty,
Osman killed them all.

759
01:15:32,840 --> 01:15:38,399
Why should I care about the lives of the men,
who are not able to live, Tendu?

760
01:15:38,960 --> 01:15:40,639
Is this why you interrupted my meal?

761
01:15:40,920 --> 01:15:43,479
We heard nothing about them, Commander Neyman.

762
01:15:44,240 --> 01:15:46,399
They still have not returned.

763
01:15:46,800 --> 01:15:50,319
They will, Tendu. They will.

764
01:15:50,400 --> 01:15:52,519
They might not return, Great Neyman.

765
01:15:52,640 --> 01:15:54,359
What does it mean?

766
01:15:54,880 --> 01:15:57,319
We've heard Osman is in Bursa.

767
01:16:02,520 --> 01:16:03,879
Osman!

768
01:16:07,400 --> 01:16:09,159
Osman!

769
01:16:12,920 --> 01:16:15,719
So, Lord has chosen his side.

770
01:16:15,920 --> 01:16:18,799
I'll bury them into the same grave!

771
01:16:18,800 --> 01:16:23,719
The ones, who are not with me,
are doomed to be destroyed!

772
01:16:26,000 --> 01:16:27,599
Get out!

773
01:16:35,640 --> 01:16:37,879
My Sultan, here.

774
01:16:43,040 --> 01:16:45,799
What are these names, Osman Bey?

775
01:16:45,920 --> 01:16:48,599
Soon, we'll have a great battle.

776
01:16:48,680 --> 01:16:50,919
These are the names of the commanders.

777
01:16:51,280 --> 01:16:56,719
My Sultan. When I appear in the battlefield,
I don't want to see these commanders in front of me.

778
01:16:58,880 --> 01:17:05,679
Who would obey a dethroned Sultan while
there is an actual Sultan, Osman Bey?

779
01:17:05,840 --> 01:17:07,759
No, my Sultan.

780
01:17:07,880 --> 01:17:12,759
Konur, who is one of my most skilled Alps,
will be also with you. Don't worry.

781
01:17:12,840 --> 01:17:15,959
He was a comrade in arms of the
many commanders here.

782
01:17:18,280 --> 01:17:21,919
Of course, everyone has a difficult job, my Sultan.

783
01:17:21,920 --> 01:17:28,919
Just convince a couple of Mother Sultan's
commanders, the rest will come.

784
01:17:29,440 --> 01:17:31,599
When the fight begins...

785
01:17:31,920 --> 01:17:34,999
...commanders will side with you Osman Bey.

786
01:17:35,000 --> 01:17:36,599
Don't worry.

787
01:17:37,200 --> 01:17:39,959
Those who are against you
in the battlefield...

788
01:17:41,000 --> 01:17:44,239
...will side with you in Konya my Sultan.

789
01:17:48,920 --> 01:17:50,719
Tomorrow will be tough.

790
01:18:07,400 --> 01:18:08,439
Alps!

791
01:18:08,840 --> 01:18:10,839
Search everywhere!

792
01:18:10,840 --> 01:18:12,839
You know what to look for.

793
01:18:13,120 --> 01:18:15,639
Look under every stone!

794
01:18:23,920 --> 01:18:24,639
Mother?

795
01:18:26,120 --> 01:18:26,839
Aunt?

796
01:18:27,480 --> 01:18:28,519
What's going on?

797
01:18:29,400 --> 01:18:31,319
What do you want Hatuns?

798
01:18:32,240 --> 01:18:34,639
Do you think this is the enemy's base?

799
01:18:34,640 --> 01:18:37,599
You know well what we want Bengi Hatun.

800
01:18:38,520 --> 01:18:41,279
First tell me what you want.

801
01:18:41,280 --> 01:18:43,199
This is not a common house.

802
01:18:43,720 --> 01:18:45,199
We want this Bengi.

803
01:18:45,320 --> 01:18:46,039
This.

804
01:18:48,840 --> 01:18:51,839
Someone changed the raw materials of the coins.

805
01:18:54,120 --> 01:18:55,919
And you thought...

806
01:18:56,600 --> 01:18:57,719
..the one who did

807
01:18:58,800 --> 01:19:00,799
...must be Bengi?

808
01:19:02,480 --> 01:19:04,879
It's nothing to be shocked about Bengi Hatun.

809
01:19:04,880 --> 01:19:06,799
You betrayed us many times before.

810
01:19:07,240 --> 01:19:08,799
That is past, Malhun Hatun.

811
01:19:09,200 --> 01:19:10,799
We're a family now.

812
01:19:11,120 --> 01:19:12,799
Yes I made a mistake.

813
01:19:13,240 --> 01:19:16,599
But you can't blame me for everything.

814
01:19:16,840 --> 01:19:18,079
My mother's right.

815
01:19:18,400 --> 01:19:20,599
Why didn't you tell us about this before?

816
01:19:21,120 --> 01:19:22,599
We're not the enemy.

817
01:19:23,400 --> 01:19:25,039
This feels like a raid.

818
01:19:25,040 --> 01:19:27,039
This is about state affairs Alcicek.

819
01:19:27,400 --> 01:19:29,359
We didn't want this either.

820
01:19:29,800 --> 01:19:32,919
But the evidence leads us here.

821
01:19:33,600 --> 01:19:34,599
Mother Bengi.

822
01:19:35,560 --> 01:19:37,259
Is there anything you want to say?

823
01:19:42,000 --> 01:19:45,799
I am innocent on this matter.

824
01:19:47,600 --> 01:19:48,799
I didn't do anything.

825
01:19:50,000 --> 01:19:51,519
Let them search.

826
01:19:55,240 --> 01:19:56,639
But...

827
01:19:57,640 --> 01:19:59,599
...if you're wrong...

828
01:20:01,520 --> 01:20:02,719
...than this is...

829
01:20:03,680 --> 01:20:06,119
...going to be your fault.

830
01:20:08,000 --> 01:20:10,959
Alps! Search everywhere!

831
01:20:46,640 --> 01:20:49,159
NAYMAN'S BASE

832
01:20:50,080 --> 01:20:52,199
Come on.
You must work!

833
01:20:52,200 --> 01:20:54,199
You must work for food!

834
01:21:01,880 --> 01:21:02,879
You!

835
01:21:03,160 --> 01:21:05,079
Teach them.
Go on!

836
01:21:09,720 --> 01:21:12,639
So you're building catapults.

837
01:21:41,240 --> 01:21:42,159
You.

838
01:21:42,200 --> 01:21:44,639
Why are you stopping?
Get to work!

839
01:21:57,120 --> 01:22:00,719
These catapults will be your end Nayman.

840
01:22:07,080 --> 01:22:09,799
Won't you say something Aktemur?

841
01:22:09,800 --> 01:22:12,399
They're doing their job.

842
01:22:13,000 --> 01:22:15,239
Don't say anything, let us wait.

843
01:22:15,880 --> 01:22:17,399
That's enough.

844
01:22:17,400 --> 01:22:19,599
We always say nothing.

845
01:22:20,800 --> 01:22:23,079
Let me tell you this.

846
01:22:24,480 --> 01:22:26,199
My dad is gone.

847
01:22:26,200 --> 01:22:27,919
I only have my mother.

848
01:22:27,920 --> 01:22:30,439
If they can't find
what they are looking for...

849
01:22:30,440 --> 01:22:32,999
If they're scapegoating my mother
for nothing then...

850
01:22:33,000 --> 01:22:34,809
...I won't stay silent this time Aktemur.

851
01:22:34,809 --> 01:22:35,879
Know that.

852
01:23:01,280 --> 01:23:03,399
Malhun Hatun.

853
01:23:04,520 --> 01:23:07,559
Your alps didn't find anything.

854
01:23:07,560 --> 01:23:09,079
We'll see Bengi Hatun.

855
01:23:09,080 --> 01:23:10,919
We'll see.

856
01:23:10,920 --> 01:23:13,119
It's apparent.

857
01:23:13,120 --> 01:23:14,639
What you're looking for is not here.

858
01:23:14,800 --> 01:23:17,319
I don't have anything to do with this either.

859
01:23:17,320 --> 01:23:20,719
Whomever told you this has lied.

860
01:23:20,720 --> 01:23:23,399
We're related now Bengi Hatun.

861
01:23:24,160 --> 01:23:26,599
We don't want to come here
like this either but...

862
01:23:26,600 --> 01:23:31,239
...the information we got says
that you're behind this.

863
01:23:33,000 --> 01:23:34,599
Then..

864
01:23:34,600 --> 01:23:37,959
..tell me who accused me.

865
01:23:37,960 --> 01:23:39,999
So that I can punish them.

866
01:23:40,000 --> 01:23:42,399
It's a secret Hatun

867
01:23:42,600 --> 01:23:45,599
Don't you know how state works at all?

868
01:23:46,000 --> 01:23:49,279
We trust the person who gave us
this information fully.

869
01:23:49,280 --> 01:23:51,479
Now tell me.

870
01:23:51,480 --> 01:23:53,319
Did you do this?

871
01:23:53,320 --> 01:23:55,759
You trust them fully...

872
01:23:55,760 --> 01:23:58,839
...but you don't trust me is that so?

873
01:23:59,880 --> 01:24:01,599
What a shame.

874
01:24:03,200 --> 01:24:07,599
I don't have anything else to
say about this matter.

875
01:24:12,840 --> 01:24:13,669
Malhun Hatun.

876
01:24:13,800 --> 01:24:15,999
We searched everywhere, there's nothing.

877
01:24:21,920 --> 01:24:25,079
Isn't it enough that you accused
my mother of being guilty?

878
01:24:25,360 --> 01:24:26,999
Yes it's true.

879
01:24:27,000 --> 01:24:29,719
She made mistakes before.

880
01:24:29,920 --> 01:24:32,999
But she went back from those mistakes.

881
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:41,839
Why are you silent?

882
01:24:41,840 --> 01:24:42,999
Speak.

883
01:24:43,000 --> 01:24:45,479
Lower your voice first.

884
01:24:49,550 --> 01:24:51,999
Then listen to us Alcicek.

885
01:24:52,000 --> 01:24:54,079
There are things you don't know.

886
01:24:54,080 --> 01:24:57,479
We didn't come here with
useless information.

887
01:24:58,960 --> 01:25:01,079
Then who said what?

888
01:25:01,320 --> 01:25:02,679
Let us know too.

889
01:25:03,200 --> 01:25:04,599
Alcicek.

890
01:25:05,320 --> 01:25:06,439
No.

891
01:25:06,880 --> 01:25:09,919
It's my turn to talk this time.

892
01:25:13,680 --> 01:25:16,999
Didn't my mother aid you
during your hardest times?

893
01:25:17,000 --> 01:25:19,319
Didn't she save your lives?

894
01:25:19,320 --> 01:25:20,679
Bala Hatun?

895
01:25:22,440 --> 01:25:24,879
Is this how you repay her?

896
01:25:27,200 --> 01:25:29,679
Alcicek!

897
01:25:30,680 --> 01:25:32,399
I said enough.

898
01:25:32,640 --> 01:25:35,119
Let her speak, Aktemur.

899
01:25:35,760 --> 01:25:38,999
She's speaking the truth.

900
01:25:39,560 --> 01:25:42,559
We do owe you a life..

901
01:25:42,920 --> 01:25:47,359
...but that debt will not alter
our sense of justice, Alcicek.

902
01:25:48,400 --> 01:25:50,999
That sense of justice..

903
01:25:51,240 --> 01:25:53,639
..only seems to be working on us,
Bala Hatun.

904
01:25:53,800 --> 01:25:55,239
Bengi Hatun...

905
01:25:55,840 --> 01:26:00,709
...we came here just as a precaution,
searched the place and found nothing.

906
01:26:01,320 --> 01:26:04,479
Thank Allah, the information wasn't true.

907
01:26:04,720 --> 01:26:07,559
I don't think you should further
address the matter.

908
01:26:07,640 --> 01:26:09,719
Why shouldn't I?

909
01:26:10,400 --> 01:26:13,439
You destroyed our reputation.

910
01:26:15,600 --> 01:26:17,919
We’re now leaving, Bengi.

911
01:26:18,200 --> 01:26:20,799
I hope you have no play in this.

912
01:26:21,160 --> 01:26:24,639
If you did something...

913
01:26:25,320 --> 01:26:28,399
...your punishment will be great.

914
01:26:31,760 --> 01:26:34,759
Alps! Prepare the horses.

915
01:27:11,520 --> 01:27:12,879
My Sultan...

916
01:27:13,120 --> 01:27:15,039
...the two of you
can continue from here.

917
01:27:15,400 --> 01:27:17,639
If Allah permits, you'll have no troubles.

918
01:27:18,160 --> 01:27:20,039
Thank you, Osman Bey.

919
01:27:20,320 --> 01:27:23,599
What makes Konya strong
is the heart of its commanders.

920
01:27:23,960 --> 01:27:25,559
Our cause is just.

921
01:27:25,960 --> 01:27:28,399
And they will choose to support it.

922
01:27:28,800 --> 01:27:30,199
Thank you.

923
01:27:30,400 --> 01:27:33,079
Thank you.
Be ready for a war for peace...

924
01:27:33,600 --> 01:27:35,599
...and a throne to bring justice.

925
01:27:35,800 --> 01:27:38,199
May Allah grant you with victory.

926
01:27:38,600 --> 01:27:41,079
Thanks. I hope He helps all of us.

927
01:27:41,280 --> 01:27:42,799
I hope so too.

928
01:27:56,000 --> 01:27:58,999
What now, my Bey?

929
01:27:59,720 --> 01:28:03,199
We did our moves on
Inegol and Iznik.

930
01:28:04,160 --> 01:28:06,559
It's now time for Tabriz.

931
01:28:07,800 --> 01:28:10,079
What are we going to do, my Bey?

932
01:28:10,400 --> 01:28:13,799
Gazan Khan is the only one who can
dethrone Sultan Alaeddin.

933
01:28:14,000 --> 01:28:17,839
Once they find out what we've done...

934
01:28:18,240 --> 01:28:20,999
...we'll see the outcomes.

935
01:28:22,640 --> 01:28:25,119
Which Alp will be going to Tabriz?

936
01:28:27,000 --> 01:28:29,199
Let's get to Yenisehir first...

937
01:28:29,920 --> 01:28:31,959
...and you’ll see there.

938
01:28:44,920 --> 01:28:48,599
Come here, soldier.

939
01:28:49,200 --> 01:28:51,199
Where did you take my horse?
I can't find it.

940
01:28:51,320 --> 01:28:52,719
Over there.

941
01:28:52,880 --> 01:28:54,759
Good. Soldier!

942
01:28:56,920 --> 01:28:59,839
Here you go.

943
01:29:01,400 --> 01:29:03,279
Peasant..

944
01:29:27,000 --> 01:29:29,559
Astagfirullah!

945
01:29:30,000 --> 01:29:32,039
It's a mess here.

946
01:29:32,040 --> 01:29:34,759
What's the difference between
you and animals?

947
01:29:48,400 --> 01:29:52,039
Just a set of eyes in Cavuldur...

948
01:29:54,000 --> 01:29:56,479
It is right sometimes,
wrong sometimes.

949
01:30:01,200 --> 01:30:04,279
My Creator, make Bayindir...

950
01:30:04,760 --> 01:30:06,119
...turn his back...

951
01:30:06,120 --> 01:30:06,919
...turn his back...

952
01:30:07,480 --> 01:30:10,399
Turn back and...

953
01:30:11,400 --> 01:30:13,759
Turn back, turn back and...

954
01:30:14,040 --> 01:30:16,799
Cerkutay...

955
01:30:28,920 --> 01:30:34,399
Why don't.you call me properly?
Why do you shout like this?

956
01:30:34,560 --> 01:30:35,839
Come here.

957
01:30:42,600 --> 01:30:44,759
I called you but you didn't hear.

958
01:30:47,320 --> 01:30:49,919
Take this to Osman Bey right away.

959
01:30:51,000 --> 01:30:54,399
Okay.
May Allah help you.

960
01:31:04,000 --> 01:31:08,039
Wow! Wow! Wow!

961
01:31:11,160 --> 01:31:13,799
My Bey, did you call me?

962
01:31:14,480 --> 01:31:18,039
May Allah take you to his side
as soon as possible, Huseyin.

963
01:31:18,320 --> 01:31:21,439
My Bey, I don't understand
if you say something good or bad.

964
01:31:21,800 --> 01:31:25,159
When have you understood anything anyway, Huseyin?
Come on! We're leaving!

965
01:31:28,120 --> 01:31:32,119
Defense is just as important
as attack in the battle, Alps!

966
01:31:41,000 --> 01:31:45,159
Don't forget!
Whoever sweats a lot in training...

967
01:31:45,360 --> 01:31:47,919
...bleed less in the war.

968
01:31:49,080 --> 01:31:52,679
They are more in number.
Mongol cavalry...

969
01:31:52,880 --> 01:31:54,759
...Byzantium infantries...

970
01:31:55,400 --> 01:31:57,599
They will be relentless!

971
01:31:59,560 --> 01:32:01,559
But we won't sit idle!

972
01:32:11,840 --> 01:32:14,919
Come on! Get up, Alps!
Is this all you got?

973
01:32:14,920 --> 01:32:17,079
Don't stop! Come on! Keep on!

974
01:32:21,560 --> 01:32:23,879
We will persevere in our defense.

975
01:32:24,000 --> 01:32:28,679
We won't have any martyrs
with this-defense order, InshAllah.

976
01:32:29,320 --> 01:32:32,580
And every infidel stepping on
these lands will know that...

977
01:32:32,580 --> 01:32:37,489
...if any of them takes a single step on these lands,
which we turned into our motherland with our blood...

978
01:32:37,489 --> 01:32:40,079
...we will make them
experience the hell itself!

979
01:32:40,280 --> 01:32:43,639
Come on, Alps!
Keep on! Come on

980
01:32:46,240 --> 01:32:50,479
This defense is unbreakable.
We stand like a castle, Turgut Bey.

981
01:32:50,600 --> 01:32:52,399
Thank you, Songur Agha, thank you.

982
01:32:52,399 --> 01:32:56,999
We will have many victories
with this order, Turgut Bey.

983
01:32:57,120 --> 01:33:01,519
I don't want any mistake, Gurbuz,
we'll train more.

984
01:33:02,400 --> 01:33:05,199
The motherland is inside a circle of fire.

985
01:33:05,200 --> 01:33:07,799
And an unmatched war is waiting for us.

986
01:33:07,800 --> 01:33:10,759
I won’t let any more of my valiants die!

987
01:33:17,200 --> 01:33:19,159
Come on, Alps! Come on!

988
01:33:28,240 --> 01:33:31,479
The army of the believers is
being raised, my Sheykh.

989
01:33:32,800 --> 01:33:36,959
You think while the infidels
unite the believers sit idle?

990
01:33:37,360 --> 01:33:38,999
Let them unite, of course.

991
01:33:39,560 --> 01:33:40,879
Tell me.

992
01:33:41,760 --> 01:33:43,999
What duty do you have for your Sheikh?

993
01:33:49,200 --> 01:33:50,519
My Sheikh.

994
01:33:51,240 --> 01:33:54,359
I was going to talk about this matter.

995
01:33:55,520 --> 01:33:59,799
Let the Bey order.
I'll accept it with the utmost respect.

996
01:34:00,200 --> 01:34:02,159
It is a matter of state after all.

997
01:34:02,400 --> 01:34:05,119
Astagfirullah. Astagfirullah.

998
01:34:09,520 --> 01:34:10,799
My Sheikh.

999
01:34:12,200 --> 01:34:14,719
In order to beat the enemy...

1000
01:34:15,760 --> 01:34:17,799
...you need to go to Gazan Khan.

1001
01:34:20,680 --> 01:34:23,399
He needs to make a move in Konya.

1002
01:34:24,040 --> 01:34:27,879
Or, neither will we be able to
enthrone Sultan Mesud....

1003
01:34:28,000 --> 01:34:31,999
...nor will we be able to challange the enemy.

1004
01:34:32,400 --> 01:34:35,359
Dervish will set out right away.

1005
01:34:35,440 --> 01:34:37,599
We will arrive Tebriz soon,
if Allah permits.

1006
01:34:39,440 --> 01:34:41,639
What is the gold bar for?

1007
01:34:42,920 --> 01:34:45,399
It will ease our way..

1008
01:34:45,520 --> 01:34:49,849
...and it will be the evidence for the letter,
which will be taken to Gazan Khan.

1009
01:34:51,800 --> 01:34:54,439
Alright, but...

1010
01:34:55,800 --> 01:34:57,519
...I have a condition.

1011
01:34:58,120 --> 01:35:00,079
Tell me, my Sheykh. Tell.

1012
01:35:00,600 --> 01:35:06,039
The one who sets out shall reach
his destination in the most beautiful way.

1013
01:35:08,640 --> 01:35:12,839
You'll make me do what I wanted to do earlier
with your order.

1014
01:35:16,320 --> 01:35:18,599
I'll go to Beyt-ul Haram.

1015
01:35:21,760 --> 01:35:24,719
I'll fulfill my duty of pilgrimage
to Makkah, Osman Bey.

1016
01:35:26,080 --> 01:35:28,319
My Sheykh,
include us to your prayers.

1017
01:35:29,200 --> 01:35:33,199
My Sheykh. You've shed light onto
my way all these years.

1018
01:35:33,400 --> 01:35:37,719
Pray in the shadow of the Kaaba
for our holy cause.

1019
01:35:41,200 --> 01:35:43,999
Come on, then.
I'd better hit the road!

1020
01:35:46,040 --> 01:35:48,639
The time is going against us.

1021
01:35:48,800 --> 01:35:51,439
We need to send the news
to the Dervish right away.

1022
01:35:51,440 --> 01:35:54,009
- Sure, my Sheykh, sure.
-Let's go.

1023
01:35:57,600 --> 01:35:59,679
You said nothing, Aktemur!

1024
01:36:00,040 --> 01:36:01,919
Aren't you the Bey of this tribe?

1025
01:36:02,000 --> 01:36:04,719
They searched your tribe
and you said nothing!

1026
01:36:04,800 --> 01:36:06,759
What could have I done, Alcicek?

1027
01:36:06,960 --> 01:36:10,879
They said they had information!
What if they found it in our tribe?

1028
01:36:11,080 --> 01:36:14,439
But it wasn'tJthe case!
They couldn't find anything, Aktemur!

1029
01:36:14,440 --> 01:36:18,159
They trampled us again, Aktemur!
They humiliated us again!

1030
01:36:18,160 --> 01:36:21,479
Alicicek! Pull yourself together!

1031
01:36:21,800 --> 01:36:23,879
Everyone does their duty.

1032
01:36:24,000 --> 01:36:28,239
You also know that Bengi Mother
and Ismihan are still together.

1033
01:36:28,240 --> 01:36:30,639
I know, of course! I know!

1034
01:36:30,800 --> 01:36:35,199
But why are they together?
Don't you see why my mother acts with that woman?

1035
01:36:35,200 --> 01:36:36,799
Why does she do it, then?

1036
01:36:36,800 --> 01:36:40,839
Your family!
Your family doesn't stand by my mother!

1037
01:36:40,840 --> 01:36:43,999
And my mother is looking for
someone she can lean on!

1038
01:36:54,040 --> 01:36:57,199
My children!
Calm down.

1039
01:36:57,480 --> 01:36:58,999
Daughter.

1040
01:36:59,000 --> 01:37:00,279
Aktemur.

1041
01:37:03,240 --> 01:37:04,199
Don't.

1042
01:37:04,520 --> 01:37:06,239
What can we do mother Ayse?

1043
01:37:06,240 --> 01:37:07,999
You saw what happened.

1044
01:37:08,000 --> 01:37:10,439
I only have my mother.

1045
01:37:10,440 --> 01:37:12,639
This upsets me so much.

1046
01:37:13,000 --> 01:37:15,279
I know my sweet girl.

1047
01:37:15,600 --> 01:37:17,319
But you should know that...

1048
01:37:17,800 --> 01:37:20,999
...no matter what happens
between families...

1049
01:37:21,200 --> 01:37:23,319
...don't let it trouble you.

1050
01:37:26,320 --> 01:37:29,519
Are you going to fall in the first wind?

1051
01:37:30,920 --> 01:37:34,159
You'll see many troubles and many fights.

1052
01:37:34,400 --> 01:37:36,359
Don't frown!

1053
01:37:36,360 --> 01:37:37,439
Smile.

1054
01:37:37,640 --> 01:37:40,039
Aktemur. Come on. Smile!

1055
01:37:43,480 --> 01:37:46,439
Don't just fake it.
Smile like you mean it.

1056
01:37:47,600 --> 01:37:50,039
Don't fool me.

1057
01:37:50,600 --> 01:37:52,359
I'm not a kid.

1058
01:37:52,560 --> 01:37:54,359
I said smile.

1059
01:37:59,600 --> 01:38:01,799
Did you gather around...

1060
01:38:02,440 --> 01:38:04,959
..for everyone that left?

1061
01:38:06,040 --> 01:38:08,759
This is an affair of the state.

1062
01:38:09,600 --> 01:38:10,719
And it's also..

1063
01:38:11,320 --> 01:38:12,719
Muslim's duty.

1064
01:38:42,360 --> 01:38:43,559
Father.

1065
01:38:43,840 --> 01:38:45,599
May. Allah keep you safe.

1066
01:38:45,600 --> 01:38:47,559
Come back soon, if Allah permits.

1067
01:38:48,920 --> 01:38:51,159
We're responsible for conquests sweetheart.

1068
01:38:53,200 --> 01:38:54,519
Victory...

1069
01:38:54,960 --> 01:38:57,439
....and return is only knowm by Allah.

1070
01:39:06,720 --> 01:39:08,719
May Allah keep you safe my Sheykh.

1071
01:39:09,000 --> 01:39:10,679
Thank you my shehzade.

1072
01:39:23,200 --> 01:39:24,799
May Allah keep you safe my Sheykh.

1073
01:39:25,400 --> 01:39:26,799
My shehzades.

1074
01:39:27,680 --> 01:39:29,639
Keep each other safe.

1075
01:39:31,600 --> 01:39:34,799
Always stay in the path of Allah.

1076
01:39:35,600 --> 01:39:38,759
That path will lead to victory.

1077
01:39:44,360 --> 01:39:45,479
My Sheykh.

1078
01:39:48,920 --> 01:39:50,479
May Allah protect you.

1079
01:39:51,600 --> 01:39:53,199
Thank you my girl.

1080
01:39:59,360 --> 01:40:00,599
My Sheykh.

1081
01:40:07,800 --> 01:40:09,199
Take care.

1082
01:40:09,200 --> 01:40:11,199
Thank you Osman Bey.

1083
01:40:16,280 --> 01:40:17,039
Come on.

1084
01:40:23,840 --> 01:40:24,879
Thank you.

1085
01:40:26,680 --> 01:40:28,719
May Allah protect you.

1086
01:40:28,759 --> 01:40:29,759
No!

1087
01:40:29,800 --> 01:40:31,359
May Allah protect you my Sheykh.

1088
01:40:31,600 --> 01:40:33,399
Take care my Sheykh.

1089
01:40:36,800 --> 01:40:38,119
No.

1090
01:40:38,200 --> 01:40:39,279
My Boran.

1091
01:40:40,480 --> 01:40:42,599
Believe in Allah...

1092
01:40:43,160 --> 01:40:45,199
...to keep me safe.

1093
01:40:49,400 --> 01:40:52,399
Our path is full of his protection.

1094
01:40:56,400 --> 01:40:57,439
Okay my Sheykh.

1095
01:40:57,840 --> 01:40:59,439
May Allah protect you.

1096
01:41:00,640 --> 01:41:01,599
Thank you.

1097
01:41:04,200 --> 01:41:07,239
-May Allah bless you all.
-Ameen.

1098
01:41:08,400 --> 01:41:10,999
May you always walk towards Allah.

1099
01:41:11,120 --> 01:41:12,999
Ameen.

1100
01:41:14,200 --> 01:41:15,399
May Allah keep you right.

1101
01:41:18,520 --> 01:41:20,399
Send my regards...

1102
01:41:20,400 --> 01:41:23,479
..and my advice to those
I couldn’t bid farewell.

1103
01:41:28,200 --> 01:41:29,759
If they'll walk with us in this path...

1104
01:41:30,600 --> 01:41:31,799
...they'll find us.

1105
01:41:34,160 --> 01:41:35,639
Take care.

1106
01:41:52,000 --> 01:41:53,239
Kumral.

1107
01:42:01,320 --> 01:42:02,999
Why don't you take me, my Sheikh?

1108
01:42:04,720 --> 01:42:07,239
Don't you think I am one of your Dervishes?

1109
01:42:07,640 --> 01:42:10,759
I can go because you're here Kumral.

1110
01:42:12,200 --> 01:42:15,999
How can I go if there's no one
to take care of our state?

1111
01:42:24,360 --> 01:42:26,159
In the name of Allah.

1112
01:42:34,600 --> 01:42:35,599
Now...

1113
01:42:36,600 --> 01:42:38,039
...the post is yours.

1114
01:42:40,200 --> 01:42:42,079
And the sweater is yours.

1115
01:42:44,680 --> 01:42:45,799
My Sheykh.

1116
01:42:48,960 --> 01:42:49,839
But...

1117
01:42:59,560 --> 01:43:01,759
Can I carry it?

1118
01:43:04,320 --> 01:43:05,959
If Allah permits, you can.

1119
01:43:09,240 --> 01:43:11,119
Touch people.

1120
01:43:12,680 --> 01:43:14,399
Touch many hearts.

1121
01:43:16,240 --> 01:43:18,239
We need those who have burning hearts, Kumral.

1122
01:43:20,960 --> 01:43:23,999
Even water burns for Allah my Sheykh.

1123
01:43:28,320 --> 01:43:29,519
Stay safe.

1124
01:43:36,800 --> 01:43:38,199
Take care.

1125
01:43:39,240 --> 01:43:40,399
Take care.

1126
01:43:52,600 --> 01:43:53,959
Kumral Abdal.

1127
01:44:00,440 --> 01:44:01,839
My Sheykh.

1128
01:44:19,000 --> 01:44:22,399
Let it be blessed.
Let it be blessed.

1129
01:44:24,720 --> 01:44:27,599
Your path shall be open, my Sheykh.

1130
01:44:42,240 --> 01:44:43,959
I told you.

1131
01:44:43,960 --> 01:44:45,439
Bengi Hatun.

1132
01:44:45,440 --> 01:44:47,839
I told you to take care of Esma!

1133
01:44:47,840 --> 01:44:49,959
They couldn't find anything.

1134
01:44:50,280 --> 01:44:54,679
I made them move the silver somewhere else
out of the tribe in case Esma told them.

1135
01:44:54,680 --> 01:44:56,239
Not enough!

1136
01:44:56,240 --> 01:44:58,079
That's not enough!

1137
01:44:58,480 --> 01:45:00,679
Just like how I silenced her before...

1138
01:45:00,680 --> 01:45:02,159
..I'll do now too.

1139
01:45:02,160 --> 01:45:03,719
Don't doubt it.

1140
01:45:03,720 --> 01:45:05,799
I'm going to send her away with her sibling.

1141
01:45:05,800 --> 01:45:07,799
I have it from now on.

1142
01:45:09,080 --> 01:45:11,839
If she was scared of you
like she used to be...

1143
01:45:11,840 --> 01:45:14,439
...she wouldn’t be able to
say even one word.

1144
01:45:14,440 --> 01:45:17,999
Send that Esma to me
as soon as possible.

1145
01:45:18,000 --> 01:45:19,399
I'm going to scare her.

1146
01:45:19,400 --> 01:45:21,239
I can handle it.

1147
01:45:24,600 --> 01:45:28,159
Don't make me say it twice Bengi.

1148
01:45:28,400 --> 01:45:33,519
Send that Esma to me as soon as possible.

1149
01:45:43,440 --> 01:45:44,999
Are the alps ready?

1150
01:45:45,000 --> 01:45:47,439
They will be, if Allah permits.

1151
01:45:47,440 --> 01:45:50,799
I know how that lowlife
Nayman will attack us like a rabid dog.

1152
01:45:50,800 --> 01:45:53,799
But we'll defend.
With Allah's permission we won't break down.

1153
01:45:53,800 --> 01:45:56,079
We'll take care of him.

1154
01:45:56,080 --> 01:45:58,479
Nayman is cornered.

1155
01:45:59,040 --> 01:46:02,239
The field he will be destroyed
shall be decided soon.

1156
01:46:03,040 --> 01:46:04,679
EyvAllah..

1157
01:46:17,800 --> 01:46:19,759
May I my bey?

1158
01:46:19,760 --> 01:46:22,199
Tell me. Tell me.

1159
01:46:38,680 --> 01:46:39,959
Ismihan.

1160
01:46:41,080 --> 01:46:43,519
She got suspicious of Bayindir.

1161
01:46:45,800 --> 01:46:47,759
But we won't reveal Bayindir.

1162
01:46:47,760 --> 01:46:50,279
We won't stop being cautious.

1163
01:47:07,520 --> 01:47:11,399
Cerkutay is saying that
Nayman is building catapults.

1164
01:47:13,400 --> 01:47:15,199
He even...

1165
01:47:21,000 --> 01:47:22,999
..sent the drawing of it.

1166
01:47:23,000 --> 01:47:24,599
There.

1167
01:47:30,800 --> 01:47:33,239
He's going to attack Yenisehir.

1168
01:47:40,520 --> 01:47:43,799
So he was waiting for the catapult
to be done huh?

1169
01:47:43,800 --> 01:47:47,599
Now I understand
what he was waiting for till now.

1170
01:47:51,800 --> 01:47:54,239
This catapult is huge.

1171
01:47:58,240 --> 01:48:02,119
If they take Yenisehir the beys near
the skirt will fall too Osman Bey.

1172
01:48:02,320 --> 01:48:04,319
I don't want to say it but..

1173
01:48:04,600 --> 01:48:07,599
...so will the feeling of
freedom within the Turks.

1174
01:48:10,600 --> 01:48:13,919
Will we allow the catapults
to be built my Bey?

1175
01:48:14,320 --> 01:48:16,919
As long as Cerkutay is there...

1176
01:48:16,920 --> 01:48:19,639
...we will never let that happen.

1177
01:48:19,920 --> 01:48:21,199
Cerkutay will stay there.

1178
01:48:21,200 --> 01:48:23,799
I have more orders for him.

1179
01:48:28,280 --> 01:48:30,479
Nayman...

1180
01:48:30,920 --> 01:48:34,079
We now know all the moves you made
and are going to make.

1181
01:48:34,800 --> 01:48:37,439
Let's see what you'll do now.

1182
01:48:38,600 --> 01:48:40,399
Are the catapults here?

1183
01:48:40,400 --> 01:48:42,919
They're.
They're ready.

1184
01:48:49,280 --> 01:48:51,399
There's word from the guards Nayman.

1185
01:48:51,400 --> 01:48:54,719
Osman's Sheykh Edebali
is going on a journey.

1186
01:48:54,720 --> 01:48:56,799
Osman.

1187
01:48:58,120 --> 01:48:59,839
Soldiers!

1188
01:48:59,840 --> 01:49:01,999
Get ready.

1189
01:49:02,000 --> 01:49:05,519
We're going to go and end
Osman's source of light.

1190
01:49:07,920 --> 01:49:11,719
He's trying to combine
all the catapults we have made...

1191
01:49:11,720 --> 01:49:14,199
..into one.

1192
01:49:14,800 --> 01:49:16,319
This one..

1193
01:49:16,320 --> 01:49:18,799
...worths ten of ours.

1194
01:49:18,800 --> 01:49:22,199
But to take a catapult
this big to the walls...

1195
01:49:22,200 --> 01:49:24,839
Wouldn't that be a handicap for them?

1196
01:49:25,920 --> 01:49:29,079
Nayman saw that he won't be
victorious on the battlefield.

1197
01:49:29,080 --> 01:49:30,799
As it looks...

1198
01:49:30,800 --> 01:49:34,399
...he wants to attack our castles and inns.

1199
01:49:34,680 --> 01:49:36,079
Osman Bey this...

1200
01:49:36,880 --> 01:49:39,559
This means a power we can't stand against.

1201
01:49:39,560 --> 01:49:41,839
Do you think that lowlife Nayman
will be successful?

1202
01:49:41,840 --> 01:49:44,359
No.

1203
01:49:44,360 --> 01:49:46,159
Orhan.

1204
01:49:46,160 --> 01:49:49,559
You were saying that they strengthened
Bursa's walls right?

1205
01:49:49,560 --> 01:49:51,359
Yes my bey.

1206
01:49:51,360 --> 01:49:54,399
But I also said our catapults
can't destroy it.

1207
01:49:57,000 --> 01:49:58,879
But...

1208
01:50:02,200 --> 01:50:04,799
But these can.

1209
01:50:07,360 --> 01:50:10,039
If we can destroy these catapults...

1210
01:50:10,040 --> 01:50:11,559
..and..

1211
01:50:11,560 --> 01:50:13,799
..build the same ones..

1212
01:50:13,800 --> 01:50:16,149
...then we'll be the ones
who have the advantage.

1213
01:50:16,149 --> 01:50:17,199
And therefore...

1214
01:50:17,200 --> 01:50:20,079
...Kopruhisar, Koyunhisar, Iznik...

1215
01:50:20,080 --> 01:50:22,959
and even Bursa's doors
will open up to us.

1216
01:50:23,720 --> 01:50:25,839
If Allah permits.

1217
01:50:27,400 --> 01:50:30,999
Then you're saying that we're going to
take the catapult Nayman has.

1218
01:50:31,000 --> 01:50:32,599
Yes.

1219
01:50:32,600 --> 01:50:35,559
Once Cerkutay completes
the rest of his mission...

1220
01:50:49,040 --> 01:50:50,079
My Bey.

1221
01:50:50,080 --> 01:50:52,799
Nayman has left his headquarters
with his warriors.

1222
01:50:52,800 --> 01:50:55,719
They're going towards the route
our Sheikh has taken.

1223
01:50:57,200 --> 01:51:00,119
What?

1224
01:51:00,400 --> 01:51:02,119
My Sheikh...

1225
01:51:03,000 --> 01:51:04,279
My father!

1226
01:51:04,440 --> 01:51:06,999
-Osman..
-Calm down.

1227
01:51:07,080 --> 01:51:10,759
I will destroy all of them if they hurt him.

1228
01:51:11,200 --> 01:51:12,719
I'll go with you.

1229
01:51:13,960 --> 01:51:14,959
-Boran!
-My Bey.

1230
01:51:14,960 --> 01:51:16,399
Prepare the Alps!

1231
01:51:16,680 --> 01:51:18,159
Okay, my Bey.

1232
01:51:18,400 --> 01:51:20,399
Alps, we're leaving!

1233
01:51:30,720 --> 01:51:31,719
Come on!

1234
01:51:33,400 --> 01:51:33,999
Let's go

1235
01:51:38,600 --> 01:51:41,199
I didn't come here to grow crops...

1236
01:51:43,000 --> 01:51:44,639
...I came here to fight.

1237
01:51:44,800 --> 01:51:48,239
But who are we going to side with?
That's the question.

1238
01:51:48,360 --> 01:51:53,119
Both Nayman and Osman
want us on their sides.

1239
01:51:55,120 --> 01:51:56,799
But...

1240
01:51:58,200 --> 01:52:01,679
What do they have in common?

1241
01:52:02,000 --> 01:52:05,399
Do you know that?

1242
01:52:09,760 --> 01:52:13,959
They're both greedy enough to
first ask for our support...

1243
01:52:14,800 --> 01:52:19,119
...then go after Bursa.

1244
01:52:20,200 --> 01:52:24,159
But there's something that they're missing.

1245
01:52:24,920 --> 01:52:27,239
Bursa can't be conquered.

1246
01:52:27,800 --> 01:52:30,199
There's no doubt about that.

1247
01:52:30,680 --> 01:52:34,399
Nayman says that he will march on Tabriz.

1248
01:52:34,720 --> 01:52:37,599
...once he destroys Osman.

1249
01:52:39,040 --> 01:52:41,719
Nayman is stuck here.

1250
01:52:42,080 --> 01:52:43,519
He needs us.

1251
01:52:43,720 --> 01:52:45,799
What about Osman?

1252
01:52:46,080 --> 01:52:49,599
We can destroy Osman with a single move.

1253
01:52:50,920 --> 01:52:52,519
But...

1254
01:52:53,480 --> 01:52:56,399
..if what he has said
turns out to be true...

1255
01:52:57,480 --> 01:52:59,559
...we will have strengthen Nayman.

1256
01:52:59,840 --> 01:53:02,999
Who are we going to choose?

1257
01:53:04,120 --> 01:53:06,959
Bursa, an example of balance...

1258
01:53:08,840 --> 01:53:12,479
...and a Bursa,
a place that's impenetrable.

1259
01:53:14,480 --> 01:53:17,879
I'm not going to rush to make a decision.

1260
01:53:20,120 --> 01:53:22,999
I will visit Nayman and Osman...

1261
01:53:23,320 --> 01:53:25,519
...on their own property.

1262
01:53:25,760 --> 01:53:30,199
I will see how they're doing
on their own lands...

1263
01:53:33,680 --> 01:53:36,639
..and then make a decision.

1264
01:53:40,520 --> 01:53:41,999
Welcome, Malhun Hatun

1265
01:53:42,680 --> 01:53:43,719
Thank you, Ulgen.

1266
01:53:43,840 --> 01:53:45,559
Tell Esma to come see me.

1267
01:53:45,800 --> 01:53:47,599
Esma?

1268
01:53:48,640 --> 01:53:50,439
She left.

1269
01:53:50,680 --> 01:53:52,319
Where did she go?

1270
01:53:52,920 --> 01:53:53,919
To Sogut.

1271
01:53:54,080 --> 01:53:55,999
Alcicek called her there.

1272
01:53:57,360 --> 01:54:00,079
What business Alcicek might
possibly have there?

1273
01:54:02,160 --> 01:54:04,319
Did she go on her own?

1274
01:54:04,800 --> 01:54:06,199
Oh, Esma

1275
01:54:06,400 --> 01:54:08,999
I told you not to trust anyone!

1276
01:54:09,400 --> 01:54:12,159
Alps, prepare my horse!

1277
01:54:24,760 --> 01:54:27,999
What is Alcicek Hatun doing in Sogut?

1278
01:54:28,400 --> 01:54:30,399
Why did you call me here?

1279
01:54:30,800 --> 01:54:33,159
I don't know about that, sister Esma.

1280
01:54:34,720 --> 01:54:37,639
Go away.
So, Esma...

1281
01:54:37,920 --> 01:54:39,799
Bengi Hatun...

1282
01:54:40,360 --> 01:54:42,599
Why couldn't you keep your mouth shut?

1283
01:54:44,400 --> 01:54:46,479
What are you going to do to me?

1284
01:54:46,600 --> 01:54:48,199
Why would I do anything?

1285
01:54:48,520 --> 01:54:51,519
Mother Sultan called you here.

1286
01:54:52,120 --> 01:54:54,639
But you need to listen to me first.

1287
01:54:54,920 --> 01:54:58,319
Just agree to everything
Mother Sultan has to say.

1288
01:54:58,920 --> 01:55:00,799
Okay?

1289
01:55:01,920 --> 01:55:04,679
I will make sure you and
your sister get away from here.

1290
01:55:04,800 --> 01:55:06,839
Don't do this, Bengi Hatun.

1291
01:55:07,280 --> 01:55:08,359
Don t do this.

1292
01:55:08,560 --> 01:55:10,599
Don't be afraid.

1293
01:55:11,320 --> 01:55:14,599
Just do what I told you to do...

1294
01:55:15,240 --> 01:55:17,719
...and agree to what Mother Sultan says.

1295
01:55:19,800 --> 01:55:22,199
Okay, daughter?

1296
01:55:23,040 --> 01:55:24,639
Okay.

1297
01:55:26,920 --> 01:55:28,239
Let’s go.

1298
01:55:54,600 --> 01:55:56,959
Protect our Sheikh!

1299
01:56:04,880 --> 01:56:07,919
They are too many of them,
my Sheykh! Get away from here.

1300
01:56:09,520 --> 01:56:10,999
We're not going to run!

1301
01:56:11,200 --> 01:56:14,079
We're going to fight back!

1302
01:56:33,840 --> 01:56:37,319
Today is the day we become martyrs!

1303
01:56:42,760 --> 01:56:43,999
Attack!

1304
01:56:50,720 --> 01:56:52,439
Allah is Everlasting!

1305
01:58:20,400 --> 01:58:23,359
Are you afraid of me, Esma?

1306
01:58:30,280 --> 01:58:31,719
You are.

1307
01:58:33,000 --> 01:58:34,319
You are, of course.

1308
01:58:35,560 --> 01:58:38,319
Then, why couldn't you hold your tongue?

1309
01:58:39,120 --> 01:58:42,719
Why did you tell
everything you see to Malhun?

1310
01:58:43,000 --> 01:58:47,079
She'll say nothing about this matter
from now on, my Sultan.

1311
01:58:47,400 --> 01:58:49,759
And she'll avoid Malhun.

1312
01:58:50,200 --> 01:58:53,079
And I'll send her away from here.

1313
01:58:54,160 --> 01:58:55,839
Right, Esma?

1314
01:58:57,920 --> 01:58:58,919
Yes.

1315
01:59:00,280 --> 01:59:03,639
I made a mistake. I owed Malhun Hatun.

1316
01:59:03,800 --> 01:59:06,079
I owed for the life of Orhan Bey.

1317
01:59:07,120 --> 01:59:09,079
I did it for it, or...

1318
01:59:20,520 --> 01:59:24,599
Osman rebels, Esma.

1319
01:59:25,120 --> 01:59:30,039
I rule over these lands, not him.

1320
01:59:36,960 --> 01:59:38,959
And what is he doing?

1321
01:59:40,920 --> 01:59:46,199
He dares to make coins
without my permission!

1322
01:59:46,800 --> 01:59:49,199
You think I can allow this?

1323
01:59:59,320 --> 02:00:01,799
Does this dagger belong to you?

1324
02:00:05,000 --> 02:00:07,319
It's a gift from Malhun Hatun.

1325
02:00:12,440 --> 02:00:14,879
Can I come in, Mother Sultan?

1326
02:00:15,680 --> 02:00:17,479
Come in, Celali.

1327
02:00:24,800 --> 02:00:27,199
Malhun Hatun is coming, my Sultan.

1328
02:00:32,000 --> 02:00:33,199
Celali.

1329
02:00:34,400 --> 02:00:35,999
Bengi Hatun.

1330
02:00:36,720 --> 02:00:38,719
You go out.

1331
02:00:41,800 --> 02:00:44,999
I said go out, Bengi Hatun.

1332
02:00:49,440 --> 02:00:52,039
Come on, Hatun! Didn't you hear?

1333
02:01:21,480 --> 02:01:23,799
So, it was a gift for your talking.

1334
02:01:39,400 --> 02:01:41,039
Seems like expensive.

1335
02:01:45,400 --> 02:01:47,479
Befits to Malhun.

1336
02:01:58,560 --> 02:02:01,759
Mother Sultan! What have you done?

1337
02:02:01,920 --> 02:02:03,199
What have you..

1338
02:02:03,960 --> 02:02:05,359
..done?

1339
02:02:13,120 --> 02:02:14,399
Ismihan.

1340
02:02:17,560 --> 02:02:19,759
Ismihan Sultan.

1341
02:03:01,360 --> 02:03:02,959
Come here Malhun.

1342
02:03:04,520 --> 02:03:05,399
Come.

1343
02:03:15,200 --> 02:03:15,999
Mother-

1344
02:03:23,520 --> 02:03:24,519
Esma.

1345
02:03:24,920 --> 02:03:26,479
Esma what happened?

1346
02:03:27,080 --> 02:03:29,959
Hang on.

1347
02:03:34,160 --> 02:03:36,479
Hang on Esma. Hang on. Hang on.

1348
02:03:39,680 --> 02:03:41,359
Hang on Esma.

1349
02:03:42,800 --> 02:03:44,199
Esma.

1350
02:03:44,200 --> 02:03:45,919
I bear witness that..

1351
02:03:46,800 --> 02:03:48,639
...there is none worthy of worship except Allah.

1352
02:03:49,160 --> 02:03:50,439
Esma.

1353
02:03:50,800 --> 02:03:52,919
I bear witness that..

1354
02:03:55,080 --> 02:03:56,999
...Mohammad is His servant and messenger.

1355
02:04:07,240 --> 02:04:08,199
Esma.

1356
02:04:11,720 --> 02:04:12,399
Ismihan.

1357
02:04:16,160 --> 02:04:17,439
Ismihan Sultan.

1358
02:04:22,400 --> 02:04:23,799
Ismihan Sultan.

1359
02:04:26,480 --> 02:04:29,919
Ismihan Sultan.

1360
02:04:47,320 --> 02:04:48,439
Malhun Hatun.

1361
02:04:51,600 --> 02:04:52,799
What have you done

1362
02:05:01,400 --> 02:05:02,879
Soldiers!

1363
02:05:02,920 --> 02:05:04,919
Arrest Malhun Hatun

1364
02:05:28,200 --> 02:05:30,759
You'll die today Edebali.

1365
02:05:31,000 --> 02:05:32,999
And Islam will die with you.

1366
02:05:33,000 --> 02:05:34,719
Death is our Shahada!

1367
02:06:03,560 --> 02:06:04,959
I'm here my Sheykh!

1368
02:06:18,480 --> 02:06:21,239
Thank Allah.

1369
02:06:23,000 --> 02:06:24,279
Allah.

1370
02:06:25,640 --> 02:06:27,159
Allah, in the name of Allah.

1371
02:06:27,160 --> 02:06:28,999
Allah.

1372
02:08:11,000 --> 02:08:12,239
My Sheykh.

1373
02:08:13,000 --> 02:08:14,719
Shaman.

1374
02:08:14,720 --> 02:08:15,919
Come here.

1375
02:08:17,600 --> 02:08:19,679
Shaman or whatever you are!

1376
02:08:20,400 --> 02:08:21,599
Come here.

1377
02:08:24,080 --> 02:08:26,239
Shaman.

1378
02:08:28,200 --> 02:08:28,999
Get up.

1379
02:08:33,960 --> 02:08:35,519
Leave, great Nayman!

1380
02:08:35,520 --> 02:08:36,599
Shaman.

1381
02:08:36,600 --> 02:08:40,279
Tengri(Turkish-Mongolian God)
will bless you with revenge.

1382
02:08:43,600 --> 02:08:47,239
So you tried to kill my Khan, my Sheykh.

1383
02:08:47,920 --> 02:08:50,599
I am going to be your wrath now.

1384
02:08:56,600 --> 02:09:00,519
So you tried to end the source of my light?

1385
02:09:03,120 --> 02:09:04,959
Here you go.

1386
02:09:12,640 --> 02:09:15,479
I'm going to take you darkness from you.

1387
02:09:15,480 --> 02:09:17,999
Osman don't.

1388
02:09:21,000 --> 02:09:22,999
Shaman.

1389
02:09:25,920 --> 02:09:32,239
I swear for this I'm going to take your
people from you Osman.

1390
02:09:33,960 --> 02:09:37,839
I'm going to take those you love from you.

1391
02:09:37,840 --> 02:09:39,799
Do your best.

1392
02:09:39,920 --> 02:09:41,399
Soldiers!

1393
02:09:41,400 --> 02:09:42,999
We're going back!

1394
02:09:43,000 --> 02:09:44,799
Move.

1395
02:09:51,800 --> 02:09:53,079
My Sheykh.

1396
02:09:54,360 --> 02:09:56,599
It's not important Osman Bey.

1397
02:09:56,600 --> 02:09:58,839
It will just make me perform ablution at best.

1398
02:09:58,840 --> 02:10:00,719
My Sheykh.

1399
02:10:01,000 --> 02:10:02,679
Father don't travel like this.

1400
02:10:02,680 --> 02:10:04,879
Let's go to Yeniseh
and get it checked.

1401
02:10:05,040 --> 02:10:07,919
There's no turning back now, my child.

1402
02:10:08,320 --> 02:10:09,319
We’ll keep going.

1403
02:10:09,440 --> 02:10:13,479
I was afraid that you'd leave
without saying goodbye, my Sheykh.

1404
02:10:13,800 --> 02:10:15,759
But seeing you now makes me feel good.

1405
02:10:16,200 --> 02:10:19,799
He who wanted to say goodbye
should have found me before I left.

1406
02:10:20,280 --> 02:10:21,559
There's no goodbye after that.

1407
02:10:21,760 --> 02:10:26,359
He who finds us on the road
can only be a comrade.

1408
02:10:36,560 --> 02:10:38,599
My Sheykh...

1409
02:10:39,520 --> 02:10:40,999
...is that what you wish?

1410
02:10:45,480 --> 02:10:48,039
What is it, Osman Bey?

1411
02:10:48,800 --> 02:10:52,439
It's whatever my Sheykh says, Turgut Bey.

1412
02:10:52,680 --> 02:10:57,079
If you wish to go with him...

1413
02:10:57,600 --> 02:10:59,399
...I'd feel good about his well-being.

1414
02:10:59,720 --> 02:11:02,479
I would feel at ease.

1415
02:11:04,600 --> 02:11:07,399
I only have one condition..

1416
02:11:10,960 --> 02:11:13,689
Do you give your blesings to
Turgur Bey, brother?

1417
02:11:18,760 --> 02:11:20,939
I do.

1418
02:11:21,880 --> 02:11:23,439
You give me your blessings too.

1419
02:11:23,600 --> 02:11:26,079
You'll always have my blessings.

1420
02:11:26,520 --> 02:11:30,799
Our tribe owes you a lot.

1421
02:11:31,000 --> 02:11:33,079
I'm always at my homeland's service.

1422
02:11:33,920 --> 02:11:36,879
Now, it seems that,
I'll oversee this mission...

1423
02:11:37,480 --> 02:11:39,479
..while you oversee home, brother.

1424
02:11:39,800 --> 02:11:41,159
Eyvallah.

1425
02:11:42,800 --> 02:11:44,399
Good luck.

1426
02:11:44,560 --> 02:11:46,159
Eyvallah.

1427
02:11:46,720 --> 02:11:48,519
Will you give me your blessings, alps?

1428
02:11:48,720 --> 02:11:50,679
We will, my Bey!

1429
02:11:51,240 --> 02:11:53,039
Brother..

1430
02:11:58,800 --> 02:12:01,599
Let’s go.
Farewell.

1431
02:12:04,720 --> 02:12:08,559
Farewell, farewell.

1432
02:12:48,000 --> 02:12:49,639
My Sheykh

1433
02:13:04,560 --> 02:13:09,359
Mother Sultan arrested
Malhun Hatun, my Bey.

1434
02:13:10,480 --> 02:13:11,879
For what reason?

1435
02:13:12,160 --> 02:13:16,119
They say that she tried to kill her.

1436
02:13:19,520 --> 02:13:22,399
What?

1437
02:13:23,480 --> 02:13:26,599
They're attacking us from all sides!

1438
02:13:27,000 --> 02:13:32,399
I will cut the tongue that lies
about my family, my Hatun!

1439
02:13:33,480 --> 02:13:35,479
It is a matter of time!

1440
02:13:36,160 --> 02:13:38,839
All of them will share the same end!

1441
02:13:39,720 --> 02:13:41,319
Alps!

1442
02:13:41,660 --> 02:13:43,520
Bring my horse!

1443
02:13:45,491 --> 02:13:54,061
Visit our website for more: turkision.com